<urn:tdn:csfc:msc:roles> tdn:theoryVersion "v3.1" .
tdn:ExtractedRole rdf:type owl:Class .
tdn:ExtractedRole rdfs:comment "Analyst-defined organizational superclass for realizations of the role and concept categories extracted from the CSfC MSC v1.3.0 source. Each role class denotes the entities or bearers that realize its source-context category. The categories include devices, services, aggregates, mixed authorities, and protocol functions. The root does not reproduce a CP definition and does not assert that every category is a physical device or an MSC Solution Component. Classes without a curated parent receive a generated organizational edge to the root; that edge is separate from source-backed subtype evidence." .
tdn:ExtractedRole rdfs:label "Extracted role or concept realization" .
tdn:ExtractedRole tdn:roleId "ExtractedRole" .
tdn:ExtractedRole tdn:roleKind "analyst_organization" .
tdn:RG-001 rdfs:label "Applicable requirements and policy precedence" .
tdn:RG-001 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:216\n| 1 => external [.localPolicyAndUSGovernmentGuidance, .cnssPolicy, .policyConflictsReported]" .
tdn:RG-001 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-001 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context must contain external confirmations that local and government guidance, CNSS policy, and the duty to report policy conflicts have been met." .
tdn:RG-002 rdfs:label "Validated configuration and component modification" .
tdn:RG-002 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:217\n| 2 => each (fun device record =>\n      records.external.Confirms .evaluatedProductConfiguration\n        (.product device.id record.product record.version device.kind) ∧\n      (record.modified = true → records.external.Confirms\n        .niapModificationDoesNotAlterCertification (.component device.id)))" .
tdn:RG-002 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-002 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each component must have confirmation that its product and version match an evaluated configuration. A modified component also needs confirmation that the modification preserves certification." .
tdn:RG-003 rdfs:label "Product eligibility on the CSfC Components List" .
tdn:RG-003 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:222\n| 3 => each (fun device record => device.kind ∈\n      [.vpn, .macsec, .grayFirewall, .outerFirewall, .innerFirewall, .authenticationServer, .intrusionPrevention] →\n      records.external.Confirms .componentsListEligibility\n        (.product device.id record.product record.version device.kind))" .
tdn:RG-003 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-003 tdn:requirementTranslation "Components of the listed kinds need external confirmation that their product and version are eligible on the CSfC Components List." .
tdn:RG-004 rdfs:label "Independent product, operating-system, and cryptographic implementations" .
tdn:RG-004 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:226\n| 4 => IndependentComponents records d" .
tdn:RG-004 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:401\ndef IndependentComponents (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  ∀ inner ∈ d.devices, inner.layer = some .inner →\n    ∀ other ∈ d.devices, (d.Relevant inner.id ∨ d.Relevant other.id) →\n    other.layer = some .outer ∨ other.kind = .grayFirewall →\n    ∀ first ∈ records.components, ∀ second ∈ records.components,\n      first.component = inner.id → second.component = other.id →\n      first.physicalDevice ≠ second.physicalDevice ∧\n      (IndependentManufacturers first second ∨\n        (first.product ≠ second.product ∧ records.external.Confirms\n          .nsaIndependenceApproval (.componentPair inner.id other.id))) ∧\n      (other.layer = some .outer →\n        first.operatingSystemFamily ≠ second.operatingSystemFamily ∧\n        IndependentCryptographicLibraries records first second)" .
tdn:RG-004 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-004 tdn:requirementTranslation "Inner encryptors must use different physical devices from Outer encryptors and Gray Firewalls. The component records must show independent manufacturers, or different products with explicit NSA approval. Inner and Outer encryptors also need different operating-system families and the specified cryptographic-library independence." .
tdn:RG-005 rdfs:label "Physical separation of security components" .
tdn:RG-005 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:227\n| 5 => PhysicalRoleSeparation records d" .
tdn:RG-005 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:415\ndef PhysicalRoleSeparation (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  ∀ first ∈ records.components, ∀ second ∈ records.components,\n    first.component ≠ second.component → (d.Relevant first.component ∨ d.Relevant second.component) →\n    (d.IsLayer first.component .inner ∧ d.IsLayer second.component .outer ∨\n      d.IsDevice first.component .grayFirewall ∧\n        (d.IsLayer second.component .inner ∨ d.IsLayer second.component .outer)) →\n    first.physicalDevice ≠ second.physicalDevice" .
tdn:RG-005 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-005 tdn:requirementTranslation "An Inner and Outer encryptor must not share a physical device. A Gray Firewall must also use a physical device distinct from either encryption layer." .
tdn:RG-006 rdfs:label "Product Supply Chain Threat Assessment" .
tdn:RG-006 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:228\n| 6 => each (fun device record =>\n      records.external.Confirms .supplyChainThreatAssessment\n        (.product device.id record.product record.version device.kind) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .supplyChainMitigation\n        (.product device.id record.product record.version device.kind))" .
tdn:RG-006 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-006 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each component needs external confirmations of a supply-chain threat assessment and the required mitigation." .
tdn:RG-007 rdfs:label "Two independent encryption layers and allowed tunnel pairings" .
tdn:RG-007 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:6\ndef msc_nested_layer_protection {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (flows : List Flow) (flowOf : S → List A → S → PayloadId → Flow) (independentKeys : String → String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_nested_layer_protection { d with focus := none } model flows flowOf independentKeys" .
tdn:RG-007 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:66\ndef Primitive_msc_nested_layer_protection {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (flows : List Flow) (flowOf : S → List A → S → PayloadId → Flow) (independentKeys : String → String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  model.CoversDeployment d ∧ ArchitectureServices d ∧\n  (∀ flow ∈ flows, flow.Valid d independentKeys) ∧\n  (∀ start actions finish, model.initial start → model.system.MTr start actions finish →\n    let events := model.TraceEvents actions\n    let selectedFlow := flowOf start actions finish\n    (∀ payload network, .inject payload network ∈ events →\n      selectedFlow payload ∈ flows ∧ (selectedFlow payload).sourceNetwork = network) ∧\n    (∀ earlier later payload iface layers trafficClass,\n      events = earlier ++ [.transmit payload iface layers trafficClass] ++ later →\n      model.ProtectedPayload d payload →\n      ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.id = iface →\n      (interface.zone = .gray → selectedFlow payload ∈ flows ∧ layers = [(selectedFlow payload).innerTunnel] ∧\n        .encrypt payload (selectedFlow payload).innerTunnel ∈ earlier) ∧\n      (interface.zone = .black → selectedFlow payload ∈ flows ∧\n        layers = [(selectedFlow payload).outerTunnel, (selectedFlow payload).innerTunnel] ∧\n        Before earlier (.encrypt payload (selectedFlow payload).innerTunnel)\n          (.encrypt payload (selectedFlow payload).outerTunnel))) ∧\n    (∀ payload iface layers trafficClass, .receive payload iface layers trafficClass ∈ events →\n      model.ProtectedPayload d payload →\n      ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.id = iface → interface.zone = .black →\n      selectedFlow payload ∈ flows ∧\n      layers = [(selectedFlow payload).outerTunnel, (selectedFlow payload).innerTunnel]) ∧\n    ∀ earlier later payload network layers,\n      events = earlier ++ [.deliver payload network layers] ++ later →\n      .inject payload (selectedFlow payload).sourceNetwork ∈ earlier → CrossedBlack d earlier payload →\n      selectedFlow payload ∈ flows ∧ network = (selectedFlow payload).destinationNetwork ∧ layers = [] ∧\n      Before earlier (.decrypt payload (selectedFlow payload).outerTunnel)\n        (.decrypt payload (selectedFlow payload).innerTunnel))" .
tdn:RG-007 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-007 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every modeled trace must use the declared Inner and Outer tunnel pairing for protected Red payloads. Gray transmission carries the Inner layer; Black transmission and reception carry both layers. Inner encryption precedes Outer encryption, and receiving-side decryption removes Outer before Inner. The definition also requires complete model coverage, independent key contexts, suitable peer placement, and the required authentication and architecture services." .
tdn:RG-008 rdfs:label "Connectivity restricted to the same security level" .
tdn:RG-008 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:10\ndef msc_security_level_connectivity {S A : Type} (context : CPContext S A) : Prop :=\n  SecurityLevelConnectivityCore { context.deployment with focus := none } context.model\n    context.authenticatedInnerPairs context.establishedInnerTunnels context.requiredConnectivity\n    context.includedUnclassified ∧\n  (∃ contexts, context ∈ contexts ∧ MSCReferencesClosed contexts) ∧\n  ∀ network ∈ context.includedUnclassified, context.AllApplicableDuties (.network network)" .
tdn:RG-008 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:97\ndef SecurityLevelConnectivityCore {S A : Type} (d : Deployment)\n    (model : ExecutionModel S A) (authenticatedInnerPairs establishedInnerTunnels : List (String × String))\n    (requiredConnectivity : List (String × String)) (includedUnclassified : List String) : Prop :=\n  model.CoversDeployment d ∧\n  DedicatedInnerAssignments d.networks ∧\n  (∀ network ∈ d.networks, ∀ inner ∈ network.innerComponents,\n    ∃ device ∈ d.devices, device.id = inner ∧ device.layer = some .inner ∧\n      device.level = network.level) ∧\n  (∀ pair ∈ authenticatedInnerPairs ++ establishedInnerTunnels,\n    ∃ first ∈ d.devices, ∃ second ∈ d.devices,\n      first.id = pair.1 ∧ second.id = pair.2 ∧ first.layer = some .inner ∧\n      second.layer = some .inner ∧ first.level = second.level) ∧\n  (model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ payload source destination layers,\n    Before events (.inject payload source) (.deliver payload destination layers) →\n    ∃ first ∈ d.networks, ∃ second ∈ d.networks,\n      first.id = source ∧ second.id = destination ∧ first.level = second.level)) ∧\n  (∀ pair ∈ requiredConnectivity, ∃ start actions finish payload,\n    model.initial start ∧ model.system.MTr start actions finish ∧\n    Before (model.TraceEvents actions) (.inject payload pair.1) (.deliver payload pair.2 [])) ∧\n  ∀ network ∈ includedUnclassified,\n    (∃ red ∈ d.networks, red.id = network ∧ red.level.classification = \"unclassified\")" .
tdn:RG-008 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-008 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each Red network has dedicated Inner components with matching security levels. Authenticated Inner pairs and established Inner tunnels stay within one level, and every delivered payload stays within its source level. Required connectivity pairs must have a successful execution. Included unclassified networks also satisfy the applicable duties, and references to other MSC solutions must be accounted for." .
tdn:RG-009 rdfs:label "Gray-network control and classification boundary" .
tdn:RG-009 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:233\n| 9 => external [.trustedRedGrayControl, .grayUnclassifiedDetermination]" .
tdn:RG-009 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-009 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmation that Red and Gray networks are under trusted control and that Gray information has been classified as unclassified." .
tdn:RG-010 rdfs:label "Independently managed site administration and trust" .
tdn:RG-010 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:234\n| 10 => (records.independentlyManaged = true →\n      (∀ record ∈ records.components, ∀ connection ∈ record.managementConnections,\n        connection.crossesBlack = false) ∧\n      (∀ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.mechanism = .ipsec →\n        ∃ first ∈ records.certificates, ∃ second ∈ records.certificates,\n          first.subject = tunnel.sender ∧ second.subject = tunnel.receiver ∧\n          first.issuer ∈ second.chain ∧ second.issuer ∈ first.chain))" .
tdn:RG-010 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-010 tdn:requirementTranslation "When independently managed operation is selected, recorded management connections must stay off Black. Each IPsec tunnel's two peers must have certificate chains that trust the other's issuer." .
tdn:RG-011 rdfs:label "Central management, CA placement, and intersite protection" .
tdn:RG-011 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:241\n| 11 => CentralManagementConfiguration records d" .
tdn:RG-011 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:455\ndef CentralManagementConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  ∀ site, d.centralManagementSite = some site →\n    (∀ component ∈ d.devices, d.certificateAuthenticated component.id = true →\n      ∃ authority ∈ d.devices, authority.kind = .certificationAuthority ∧\n        authority.site = site ∧ d.keyManagementCA component.id authority.id) ∧\n    (∀ first ∈ d.devices, ∀ second ∈ d.devices,\n      first.layer = some .inner → second.layer = some .outer →\n      d.certificateAuthenticated first.id = true → d.certificateAuthenticated second.id = true →\n      ∀ firstCA secondCA, d.keyManagementCA first.id firstCA →\n        d.keyManagementCA second.id secondCA → firstCA ≠ secondCA) ∧\n    (∀ component ∈ d.devices, component.kind = .macsec →\n      d.certificateAuthenticated component.id = true →\n      ∃ server ∈ d.devices, server.kind = .authenticationServer ∧ server.site = site) ∧\n    (∀ record ∈ records.components, ∀ connection ∈ record.managementConnections,\n      connection.crossesBlack = true → 2 ≤ connection.approvedEncryptionLayers) ∧\n    (∀ record ∈ records.components, record.managementConnections ≠ [] →\n      record.managementCryptographicSeparated = true)" .
tdn:RG-011 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-011 tdn:requirementTranslation "When a central management site is declared, certificate-authenticated components need a CA at that site, and Inner and Outer components use distinct CAs. Certificate-authenticated MACsec devices also need an Authentication Server there. Recorded management connections crossing Black use at least two approved encryption layers, and components with management connections have cryptographic separation enabled." .
tdn:RG-012 rdfs:label "Separate authentication and management for security levels" .
tdn:RG-012 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/AuthenticationIsolation.lean:33\ndef msc_security_level_key_and_management_separation\n    (managementSelected : Bool) (peers : List InnerAuthentication) : Prop :=\n  (managementSelected = true → ∀ a ∈ peers, a.managementDevices.Nonempty) ∧\n  (∀ a ∈ peers, ∀ b ∈ peers, a.level ≠ b.level →\n    MaterialsSeparated a b ∧\n    (managementSelected = true → Disjoint a.managementDevices b.managementDevices) ∧\n    ¬ InnerCanAuthenticate a b)" .
tdn:RG-012 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:17\ndef msc_security_level_key_and_management_separation :=\n  Primitive_msc_security_level_key_and_management_separation" .
tdn:RG-012 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:119\ndef Primitive_msc_security_level_key_and_management_separation (managementDeployed : Bool)\n    (peers : List InnerAuthentication) (establishedTunnel : String → String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  TDN.Targets.msc_security_level_key_and_management_separation managementDeployed peers ∧\n  ∀ a ∈ peers, ∀ b ∈ peers, a.level ≠ b.level → ¬ establishedTunnel a.component b.component" .
tdn:RG-012 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-012 tdn:requirementTranslation "Inner peers at different levels must use separated authentication material, must not authenticate each other, and must have no established tunnel between them. When management is deployed, each peer has management devices and different levels use disjoint management-device sets." .
tdn:RG-013 rdfs:label "Gray Firewalls on all paths needing level separation" .
tdn:RG-013 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:20\ndef msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage (d : Deployment) (topology : GrayTopology) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage { d with focus := none } topology" .
tdn:RG-013 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:151\ndef Primitive_msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage (d : Deployment) (topology : GrayTopology) : Prop :=\n  d.AddressInventoryCoherent ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.inner node ↔ d.IsLayer node .inner) ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.grayFirewall node ↔ d.IsDevice node .grayFirewall) ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.outer node ↔ d.IsLayer node .outer) ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.workstation node ↔ d.grayWorkstation node) ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.localCA node → topology.certificationAuthority node) ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.certificationAuthority node ↔\n    d.IsDevice node .certificationAuthority ∧\n      ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.device = node ∧ interface.zone = .gray) ∧\n  (∀ node, topology.revocationService node ↔\n    d.IsDevice node .revocationService ∧\n      ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.device = node ∧ interface.zone = .gray) ∧\n  (∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → topology.level device.id = device.level) ∧\n  TDN.Targets.msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage topology.edge topology.grayFirewall topology.inner\n    (GrayManagement topology) topology.level topology.highest topology.dominates\n    (FiltersIntendedPeers d) d.authority.protectsAsClassified ∧\n  (∀ service component,\n    (topology.workstation service ∨ topology.certificationAuthority service ∨\n      topology.revocationService service) → topology.inner component →\n    topology.level service ≠ topology.level component →\n    ¬ Relation.ReflTransGen (Waypointing.Avoiding topology.edge topology.grayFirewall) service component) ∧\n  (∀ outer, topology.outer outer → FiltersIntendedPeers d outer) ∧\n  (∀ firewall, topology.grayFirewall firewall → ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device →\n    interface.device = firewall → ∀ direction traffic,\n      d.Accepts interface.id direction traffic →\n      ∀ manager component, GrayManagement topology manager → topology.inner component →\n        topology.level component ≠ topology.highest →\n        ¬ ((traffic.sourceDevice = some manager ∧ traffic.destinationDevice = some component) ∨\n          (traffic.sourceDevice = some component ∧ traffic.destinationDevice = some manager))) ∧\n  ∀ firewall, topology.grayFirewall firewall → ∃ outer inner,\n    topology.outer outer ∧ topology.inner inner ∧\n    Relation.ReflTransGen topology.edge inner firewall ∧\n    Relation.ReflTransGen topology.edge firewall outer" .
tdn:RG-013 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/Topology.lean:90\ndef msc_gray_firewall_path_coverage {Node Label : Type}\n    (grayEdge : Node → Node → Prop) (grayFirewall inner management : Node → Prop)\n    (level : Node → Label) (highest : Label) (dominates : Label → Label → Prop)\n    (filtersIntendedSameLevel physicallyProtected : Node → Prop) : Prop :=\n  (∀ a b, inner a → inner b → level a ≠ level b →\n    ¬ Relation.ReflTransGen (Waypointing.Avoiding grayEdge grayFirewall) a b) ∧\n  (∀ administrator component, management administrator → inner component →\n    level component ≠ highest →\n      ¬ Relation.ReflTransGen (Waypointing.Avoiding grayEdge grayFirewall) administrator component) ∧\n  (∀ administrator, management administrator → level administrator = highest) ∧\n  (∀ component, inner component → dominates highest (level component)) ∧\n  (∀ firewall, grayFirewall firewall →\n    filtersIntendedSameLevel firewall ∧ physicallyProtected firewall) ∧\n  ((∃ a b, inner a ∧ inner b ∧ level a ≠ level b) → ∃ firewall, grayFirewall firewall)" .
tdn:RG-013 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-013 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every Gray path that crosses the specified security-level boundary must pass through a Gray Firewall. The modeled roles and levels must match the device records. Firewalls and Outer components filter Inner peers by level; Gray management and certificate services have the stated placement and separation conditions. Each Gray Firewall must also lie on an actual Inner-to-Outer path." .
tdn:RG-014 rdfs:label "Gray addressing supports security-level filtering" .
tdn:RG-014 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:23\ndef msc_gray_addressing_for_level_filtering (d : Deployment)\n    (ranges : List (Addressing.Range SecurityLevel)) (pairs : List IntendedAddressPair) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_gray_addressing_for_level_filtering { d with focus := none } ranges pairs" .
tdn:RG-014 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:186\ndef Primitive_msc_gray_addressing_for_level_filtering (d : Deployment)\n    (ranges : List (Addressing.Range SecurityLevel)) (pairs : List IntendedAddressPair) : Prop :=\n  d.AddressInventoryCoherent ∧\n  (∀ range ∈ ranges, range.low ≤ range.high) ∧\n  (∀ address a b, Addressing.Owns ranges address a → Addressing.Owns ranges address b → a = b) ∧\n  (∀ pair ∈ pairs, Addressing.Owns ranges pair.source pair.level ∧\n    Addressing.Owns ranges pair.destination pair.level) ∧\n  (∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.zone = .gray → d.IsLayer interface.device .inner →\n    ∃ device ∈ d.devices, device.id = interface.device ∧\n      ∃ address, interface.address = some address ∧ Addressing.Owns ranges address device.level) ∧\n  ∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → device.layer = some .outer ∨ device.kind = .grayFirewall →\n    FiltersIntendedPeers d device.id ∧\n    ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.device = device.id → interface.zone = .gray →\n      ∀ direction traffic, d.Accepts interface.id direction traffic → InnerEndpoints d traffic →\n        IntendedPair pairs traffic.packet" .
tdn:RG-014 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-014 tdn:requirementTranslation "Gray address ranges must be valid and must assign an address to at most one security level. Inner Gray addresses and intended address pairs belong to the recorded level. Outer components and Gray Firewalls accept Inner-peer traffic only for the intended same-level pairs." .
tdn:RG-015 rdfs:label "MACsec encapsulation and standalone encapsulator obligations" .
tdn:RG-015 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:27\ndef msc_macsec_encapsulation {S A : Type} (context : CPContext S A) : Prop :=\n  MACsecEncapsulationCore { context.deployment with focus := none } context.model\n    context.encapsulations context.crossesIP ∧\n  ∀ use ∈ context.encapsulations, use.builtInSupported = false →\n    context.AllApplicableDuties (.component use.encapsulator)" .
tdn:RG-015 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:214\ndef MACsecEncapsulationCore {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (uses : List EncapsulationUse) (crossesIP : String → Bool) : Prop :=\n  model.CoversDeployment d ∧\n  (∀ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, (d.Relevant tunnel.sender ∨ d.Relevant tunnel.receiver) → tunnel.mechanism = .macsec →\n    tunnel.layer = .inner ∨ crossesIP tunnel.id = true →\n      ∃ use ∈ uses, use.protectedTunnel = tunnel.id ∧ use.inner = tunnel.sender ∧\n        (tunnel.layer = .inner → use.outer.isSome = true) ∧\n        (crossesIP tunnel.id = true → use.traversesIP = true)) ∧\n  (∀ use ∈ uses, (d.Relevant use.inner ∨ d.Relevant use.encapsulator ∨\n      d.Relevant use.remoteEncapsulator) →\n    d.authority.aoApprovedEncapsulation use.protocol ∧\n    (use.builtInSupported = false → d.standaloneEncapsulator use.encapsulator ∧\n      d.OwnedGrayAttachment use.inner use.encapsulator use.inputInterface ∧\n      (∀ outer, use.outer = some outer →\n        d.OwnedGrayExit use.encapsulator use.outputInterface outer))) ∧\n  model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ use ∈ uses, (d.Relevant use.inner ∨ d.Relevant use.encapsulator ∨\n      d.Relevant use.remoteEncapsulator) → ∀ payload,\n    .encrypt payload use.protectedTunnel ∈ events →\n      (∀ outer tunnel, use.outer = some outer →\n        (∃ t ∈ d.tunnels, t.id = tunnel ∧ t.sender = outer) →\n        BeforeEvery events (.encapsulate payload use.encapsulator use.protocol)\n          (.encrypt payload tunnel)) ∧\n      (use.traversesIP = true → ∀ earlier later layers trafficClass,\n        events = earlier ++ [.transmit payload use.outputInterface layers trafficClass] ++ later →\n        .encapsulate payload use.encapsulator use.protocol ∈ earlier) ∧\n      (∀ first middle last,\n        events = first ++ [.encapsulate payload use.encapsulator use.protocol] ++ middle ++\n          [.decapsulate payload use.remoteEncapsulator use.protocol] ++ last →\n        .decrypt payload use.protectedTunnel ∉ middle))" .
tdn:RG-015 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-015 tdn:requirementTranslation "Inner MACsec traffic and MACsec traffic crossing IP must have a declared, approved encapsulation arrangement. Encapsulation precedes the required Outer encryption or IP transmission, and the protected MACsec layer stays encrypted between encapsulation and decapsulation. A standalone encapsulator needs the specified Gray attachments and all applicable component duties." .
tdn:RG-016 rdfs:label "Permitted MACsec clear VLAN tags and XPN" .
tdn:RG-016 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:242\n| 16 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .macsec →\n      (record.optionalClearVLAN = true → \"clear-vlan\" ∈ record.supportedFeatures) ∧\n      (record.optionalXPN = true → \"xpn\" ∈ record.supportedFeatures))" .
tdn:RG-016 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-016 tdn:requirementTranslation "A MACsec device may select clear VLAN tags or XPN only when its recorded supported features contain the corresponding option." .
tdn:RG-017 rdfs:label "Mutual authentication and Non-Person Entity certificates" .
tdn:RG-017 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:245\n| 17 => MutuallyAuthenticatedTunnels records d" .
tdn:RG-017 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:444\ndef MutuallyAuthenticatedTunnels (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  ∀ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, (d.Relevant tunnel.sender ∨ d.Relevant tunnel.receiver) →\n    ∃ first ∈ records.authentications, ∃ second ∈ records.authentications,\n      first.input.verifier = tunnel.sender ∧ first.input.claimant = tunnel.receiver ∧\n      second.input.verifier = tunnel.receiver ∧ second.input.claimant = tunnel.sender ∧\n      first.association = tunnel.id ∧ second.association = tunnel.id ∧\n      match tunnel.mechanism with\n      | .ipsec => AuthenticatedCertificate records first ∧ AuthenticatedCertificate records second\n      | .macsec => AuthenticatedSharedKey records first tunnel.keyContext ∧\n          AuthenticatedSharedKey records second tunnel.keyContext" .
tdn:RG-017 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-017 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every relevant tunnel needs authentication observations in both directions, with each verifier authenticating the opposite peer for that tunnel. The current shared condition uses certificate authentication for IPsec and proof of possession of the tunnel key for MACsec." .
tdn:RG-018 rdfs:label "CNSS algorithm-policy requirements and choices" .
tdn:RG-018 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:246\n| 18 => each (fun device record =>\n      (device.kind = .vpn → IPsecAlgorithmConfiguration record) ∧\n      (device.kind = .macsec → record.macsecBits = 256 ∧\n        record.macsecAlgorithm ∈ [\"GCM-AES-256\", \"GCM-AES-XPN-256\"]))" .
tdn:RG-018 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:473\ndef IPsecAlgorithmConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.offeredIPsecSuites ≠ [] ∧\n  if record.cnsa2Selected then\n    (∀ suite ∈ record.offeredIPsecSuites, CNSA2IPsec suite) ∧\n    (∀ connection ∈ record.ipsecConnections,\n      connection.initial.keyEstablishment ∈ [\"ECDH-P384\", \"DH3072\", \"DH4096\"] ∧\n      connection.intermediate.keyEstablishment = \"ML-KEM-1024\" ∧\n      connection.intermediateEncrypted = true ∧ connection.multipleKeyExchanges = true ∧\n      connection.intermediateExchangeSupported = true ∧ connection.ikeFragmentationSupported = true)\n  else ∀ suite ∈ record.offeredIPsecSuites, CNSA1IPsec suite" .
tdn:RG-018 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-018 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every VPN gateway offers a nonempty set of suites satisfying the chosen CNSA profile. Selecting CNSA 2 also requires the recorded classical initial exchange and encrypted ML-KEM-1024 intermediate exchange, with multiple exchanges and IKE fragmentation supported. MACsec components use 256-bit GCM-AES or GCM-AES-XPN." .
tdn:RG-019 rdfs:label "IPsec CNSA profile and post-quantum exchange sequence" .
tdn:RG-019 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:250\n| 19 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .vpn → IPsecAlgorithmConfiguration record)" .
tdn:RG-019 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:473\ndef IPsecAlgorithmConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.offeredIPsecSuites ≠ [] ∧\n  if record.cnsa2Selected then\n    (∀ suite ∈ record.offeredIPsecSuites, CNSA2IPsec suite) ∧\n    (∀ connection ∈ record.ipsecConnections,\n      connection.initial.keyEstablishment ∈ [\"ECDH-P384\", \"DH3072\", \"DH4096\"] ∧\n      connection.intermediate.keyEstablishment = \"ML-KEM-1024\" ∧\n      connection.intermediateEncrypted = true ∧ connection.multipleKeyExchanges = true ∧\n      connection.intermediateExchangeSupported = true ∧ connection.ikeFragmentationSupported = true)\n  else ∀ suite ∈ record.offeredIPsecSuites, CNSA1IPsec suite" .
tdn:RG-019 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-019 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every VPN gateway offers at least one suite, and every offered suite meets its selected CNSA profile. CNSA 2 connections begin with ECDH-P384, DH3072, or DH4096 and use ML-KEM-1024 in an encrypted intermediate exchange. Multiple exchanges, the intermediate exchange, and IKE fragmentation must be supported." .
tdn:RG-020 rdfs:label "VPN certificate loading and authentication checks" .
tdn:RG-020 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:251\n| 20 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .vpn →\n      CertificateIdentityConfiguration records device.id record.removeDefaultCertificatesSelected)" .
tdn:RG-020 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:423\ndef CertificateIdentityConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (component : String)\n    (removeDefaults : Bool) : Prop :=\n  (∃ certificate ∈ records.certificates,\n    certificate.subject = component ∧ certificate.nonPersonEntity = true ∧\n    certificate.id ≠ \"\" ∧ certificate.trustAnchor ∈ certificate.chain ∧\n    certificate.issuer ∈ certificate.chain) ∧\n  (∀ first ∈ records.certificates, ∀ second ∈ records.certificates,\n    first.subject = component → first.id = second.id → second.subject = component) ∧\n  (∀ observation ∈ records.authentications, (observation.input.verifier = component ∨ observation.input.claimant = component) →\n    AuthenticatedCertificate records observation) ∧\n  (removeDefaults = true → ∀ certificate ∈ records.certificates,\n    certificate.subject = component →\n    certificate.vendorDefault = false ∧ certificate.selfSigned = false ∧\n      certificate.proprietary = false)" .
tdn:RG-020 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-020 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every VPN gateway has a nonempty device-certificate identity whose chain contains its issuer and trust anchor. That certificate identity cannot belong to another component. Recorded authentications involving the gateway satisfy the certificate-verification conditions. Selecting default-certificate removal excludes vendor-default, self-signed, and proprietary certificates." .
tdn:RG-021 rdfs:label "VPN private-key access confinement" .
tdn:RG-021 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:33\ndef msc_vpn_private_key_confinement {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (keys : List PrivateKey) (objectiveSelected : String → Bool)\n    (policies : List MandatoryKeyPolicy) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_vpn_private_key_confinement { d with focus := none } model keys objectiveSelected policies" .
tdn:RG-021 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:257\ndef Primitive_msc_vpn_private_key_confinement {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (keys : List PrivateKey) (objectiveSelected : String → Bool)\n    (policies : List MandatoryKeyPolicy) : Prop :=\n  StoredVPNKeyInventory d keys ∧\n  (model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ key ∈ keys, d.Relevant key.gateway → ∀ interface,\n    .privateKeyExport key.gateway key.id interface ∉ events)) ∧\n  (∀ key ∈ keys, d.Relevant key.gateway → objectiveSelected key.gateway = true → ∃ policy ∈ policies,\n    policy.gateway = key.gateway ∧ policy.enforced = true ∧\n    ∀ principal, policy.permits principal key.id → principal = key.gateway) ∧\n  model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ key ∈ keys, d.Relevant key.gateway → objectiveSelected key.gateway = true →\n    ∀ principal, .privateKeyRead key.gateway key.id principal ∈ events → principal = key.gateway)" .
tdn:RG-021 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-021 tdn:requirementTranslation "The key inventory must account for the VPN gateway's stored private keys. No modeled trace may export a listed private key. When the access-control objective is selected, an enforced policy permits only the gateway to read its key, and every modeled key read respects that restriction." .
tdn:RG-022 rdfs:label "IKEv2 and IKE/ESP encryption-mode alternatives" .
tdn:RG-022 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:253\n| 22 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .vpn → IPsecModesAndLifetimes record)" .
tdn:RG-022 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:484\ndef IPsecModesAndLifetimes (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.ikeVersion = 2 ∧\n  record.ikeMode = (if record.ikeGCMSelected then \"GCM\" else \"CBC\") ∧\n  record.espMode = (if record.espGCMSelected then \"GCM\" else \"CBC\") ∧\n  (record.espMode = \"CBC\" → record.espHMAC = true) ∧\n  0 < record.ikeLifetimeSeconds ∧ record.ikeLifetimeSeconds ≤ 86400 ∧\n  0 < record.espLifetimeSeconds ∧ record.espLifetimeSeconds ≤ 28800" .
tdn:RG-022 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-022 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every VPN gateway uses IKEv2 and the selected GCM or CBC modes. CBC for ESP requires HMAC. Recorded IKE lifetimes are positive and at most 24 hours; ESP lifetimes are positive and at most eight hours." .
tdn:RG-023 rdfs:label "VPN SA lifetimes and reauthentication" .
tdn:RG-023 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:254\n| 23 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .vpn →\n      IPsecModesAndLifetimes record ∧\n      ∀ rekey ∈ records.rekeys, rekey.device = device.id →\n        rekey.authenticatedAt < rekey.rekeyedAt ∧\n        ∃ observation ∈ records.authentications,\n          observation.input.verifier = device.id ∧ observation.input.claimant = rekey.peer ∧\n          observation.association = rekey.association ∧\n          observation.input.time = rekey.authenticatedAt ∧ AuthenticatedCertificate records observation)" .
tdn:RG-023 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:484\ndef IPsecModesAndLifetimes (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.ikeVersion = 2 ∧\n  record.ikeMode = (if record.ikeGCMSelected then \"GCM\" else \"CBC\") ∧\n  record.espMode = (if record.espGCMSelected then \"GCM\" else \"CBC\") ∧\n  (record.espMode = \"CBC\" → record.espHMAC = true) ∧\n  0 < record.ikeLifetimeSeconds ∧ record.ikeLifetimeSeconds ≤ 86400 ∧\n  0 < record.espLifetimeSeconds ∧ record.espLifetimeSeconds ≤ 28800" .
tdn:RG-023 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-023 tdn:requirementTranslation "VPN gateways satisfy the IKEv2, selected-mode, and positive lifetime limits: at most 24 hours for IKE and eight hours for ESP. Every recorded rekey follows an authenticated observation for the same gateway, peer, and association; the authentication time precedes the rekey time." .
tdn:RG-024 rdfs:label "MACsec authentication alternatives and AS scope" .
tdn:RG-024 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:38\ndef msc_macsec_authentication_choice_and_as {S A : Type} (d : Deployment)\n    (model : ExecutionModel S A) (primitive : TLSPrimitive)\n    (authentication : List MACsecAuthentication) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_macsec_authentication_choice_and_as { d with focus := none } model primitive authentication" .
tdn:RG-024 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:537\ndef Primitive_msc_macsec_authentication_choice_and_as {S A : Type} (d : Deployment)\n    (model : ExecutionModel S A) (primitive : TLSPrimitive)\n    (authentication : List MACsecAuthentication) : Prop :=\n  MACsecInstalledHistory d model primitive authentication ∧\n  (∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → device.kind = .macsec →\n    ∃ selected ∈ authentication, selected.device = device.id) ∧\n  (∀ selected ∈ authentication, (d.Relevant selected.device ∨ d.Relevant selected.server) →\n    d.IsDevice selected.device .macsec ∧ d.IsDevice selected.peer .macsec ∧\n    (selected.method = .preSharedCAK ↔ d.preSharedCAKAuthenticated selected.device = true) ∧\n    (selected.method = .eapTLS ↔ d.certificateAuthenticated selected.device = true) ∧\n    (selected.keyServer = selected.device ∨ selected.keyServer = selected.peer) ∧\n    selected.secureAssociationKey ≠ \"\" ∧\n    match selected.method with\n    | .preSharedCAK => selected.cak ≠ \"\" ∧ selected.cak = selected.peerCAK\n    | .eapTLS => d.IsDevice selected.server .authenticationServer ∧\n        selected.supportedRoles = [.supplicant, .authenticator] ∧\n        selected.deviceCertificate ≠ \"\" ∧ selected.peerCertificate ≠ \"\" ∧\n        selected.serverCertificate ≠ \"\" ∧\n        EAPEndpointRoleEvidence primitive selected ∧\n        (∃ exchange ∈ selected.exchanges, EAPSessionBinding primitive selected exchange) ∧\n        (∀ site zone, (site, zone) ∈ selected.serverAttachments ↔\n          d.networkAttachment selected.server site zone) ∧\n        (∃ site zone, selected.serverAttachments ≠ [] ∧\n          ∀ attachment ∈ selected.serverAttachments, attachment = (site, zone)) ∧\n        ∀ attachment ∈ selected.serverAttachments, attachment.2 = .red ∨ attachment.2 = .gray) ∧\n  model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ earlier later payload tunnel,\n    events = earlier ++ [.encrypt payload tunnel] ++ later →\n    ∀ configured ∈ d.tunnels, configured.id = tunnel → configured.mechanism = .macsec →\n    ∃ selected ∈ authentication, selected.device = configured.sender ∧\n      selected.peer = configured.receiver ∧\n      MACsecKeyUsePrefix primitive selected payload tunnel earlier)" .
tdn:RG-024 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-024 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each MACsec device must have a declared authentication choice and peer. A pre-shared CAK must match the peer's CAK. EAP-TLS requires the device, peer, and server certificates, the supported endpoint roles, session evidence, and an Authentication Server attached to one Red or Gray site-and-zone pair. Installed keys and every encryption use must be connected to the required earlier authentication and key setup." .
tdn:RG-025 rdfs:label "MACsec encryption and key wrapping algorithms" .
tdn:RG-025 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:262\n| 25 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .macsec →\n      record.keyWrapAlgorithm = \"AES-Key-Wrap\" ∧ record.keyWrapBits = 256 ∧\n      record.macsecBits = 256 ∧ record.macsecAlgorithm ∈ [\"GCM-AES-256\", \"GCM-AES-XPN-256\"])" .
tdn:RG-025 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-025 tdn:requirementTranslation "MACsec encryption uses 256-bit GCM-AES or GCM-AES-XPN, and key wrapping uses 256-bit AES-Key-Wrap." .
tdn:RG-026 rdfs:label "MACsec EAP-TLS CNSA profile alternatives" .
tdn:RG-026 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:265\n| 26 => each (fun device record =>\n      (device.kind = .macsec ∧ d.certificateAuthenticated device.id = true ∨\n        device.kind = .authenticationServer) → EAPAlgorithmConfiguration record)" .
tdn:RG-026 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:492\ndef EAPAlgorithmConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.offeredEAPSuites ≠ [] ∧\n  if record.eapCNSA2Selected then record.eapTLSVersionMajor = 1 ∧\n    record.eapTLSVersionMinor = 3 ∧\n    ∀ suite ∈ record.offeredEAPSuites, CNSA2EAP suite\n  else ∀ suite ∈ record.offeredEAPSuites, CNSA1EAP suite" .
tdn:RG-026 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-026 tdn:requirementTranslation "Certificate-authenticated MACsec devices and Authentication Servers offer a nonempty set of EAP-TLS suites, all satisfying the selected CNSA profile. Selecting CNSA 2 requires TLS 1.3." .
tdn:RG-027 rdfs:label "MACsec key generation, key-server selection, and rollover" .
tdn:RG-027 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:43\ndef msc_macsec_key_generation_and_server (d : Deployment) (keys : List MACsecKey)\n    (pairs : List MACsecServerPair) (provisioning : List KeyProvisioning)\n    (eapCAKGeneratedByApprovedKGS : String → String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_macsec_key_generation_and_server { d with focus := none } keys pairs provisioning\n    eapCAKGeneratedByApprovedKGS" .
tdn:RG-027 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:596\ndef Primitive_msc_macsec_key_generation_and_server (d : Deployment) (keys : List MACsecKey)\n    (pairs : List MACsecServerPair) (provisioning : List KeyProvisioning)\n    (eapCAKGeneratedByApprovedKGS : String → String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  (∀ key ∈ keys, d.RelevantKey key.cak → 16 ≤ key.ckn.length ∧ d.authority.nsaApprovedGenerator key.cknGenerator ∧\n    (match key.cakOrigin with\n      | .generated generator => d.authority.nsaApprovedGenerator generator ∧\n          ∃ provision ∈ provisioning, provision.key = key.cak ∧ provision.generator = generator ∧\n            d.authority.securityAdministrator provision.administrator ∧\n            ∀ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, (d.Relevant tunnel.sender ∨ d.Relevant tunnel.receiver) → tunnel.mechanism = .macsec → tunnel.keyContext = key.cak →\n              (∃ applied ∈ provision.applications, applied.1 = tunnel.sender ∧\n                provision.obtainedOrder < applied.2) ∧\n              ∃ applied ∈ provision.applications, applied.1 = tunnel.receiver ∧\n                provision.obtainedOrder < applied.2\n      | .eapDerived msk => msk ≠ \"\" ∧ ∃ generator, d.authority.nsaApprovedGenerator generator ∧\n          eapCAKGeneratedByApprovedKGS key.cak generator) ∧ key.fallbackEnabled = false) ∧\n  (∀ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, (d.Relevant tunnel.sender ∨ d.Relevant tunnel.receiver) → tunnel.mechanism = .macsec →\n    (∃ key ∈ keys, key.cak = tunnel.keyContext) ∧\n    ∃ pair ∈ pairs, pair.first = tunnel.sender ∧ pair.second = tunnel.receiver) ∧\n  ∀ pair ∈ pairs, (d.Relevant pair.first ∨ d.Relevant pair.second) → pair.centralSite = d.centralManagementSite ∧ pair.first ≠ pair.second ∧\n    ((pair.firstValue = 0 ∧ pair.secondValue = 1) ∨\n      (pair.firstValue = 1 ∧ pair.secondValue = 0)) ∧\n    ∀ site, pair.centralSite = some site →\n      (∃ first ∈ d.devices, first.id = pair.first ∧ first.site = site ∧ pair.firstValue = 0) ∨\n      (∃ second ∈ d.devices, second.id = pair.second ∧ second.site = site ∧ pair.secondValue = 0)" .
tdn:RG-027 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-027 tdn:requirementTranslation "Relevant MACsec keys use the required key-name length and approved generation records, with fallback disabled. Generated CAKs must be obtained by an authorized administrator before application to both peers; EAP-derived CAKs need the required generator evidence. Every MACsec tunnel has a key and peer-pair record. The peers have complementary key-server values, and a centrally managed pair gives value 0 to a peer at the central site." .
tdn:RG-028 rdfs:label "MACsec mandatory protection parameters" .
tdn:RG-028 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:49\ndef msc_macsec_protection_parameters {S A : Type} (d : Deployment)\n    (model : ExecutionModel S A) (parameters : List MACsecParameters) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_macsec_protection_parameters { d with focus := none } model parameters" .
tdn:RG-028 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:632\ndef Primitive_msc_macsec_protection_parameters {S A : Type} (d : Deployment)\n    (model : ExecutionModel S A) (parameters : List MACsecParameters) : Prop :=\n  model.CoversDeployment d ∧\n  (∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → device.kind = .macsec →\n    ∃ parameter ∈ parameters, parameter.device = device.id) ∧\n  (∀ parameter ∈ parameters, d.Relevant parameter.device → parameter.dataDelayProtection = true ∧\n    parameter.lifetimeMilliseconds = 6000 ∧ parameter.normalHelloMilliseconds = 2000 ∧\n    0 < parameter.activeHelloMilliseconds ∧ parameter.activeHelloMilliseconds ≤ 2000 ∧\n    (parameter.replayWindow = 2 ∨ (parameter.feasibleReplayWindow parameter.replayWindow ∧\n      ∀ feasible, parameter.feasibleReplayWindow feasible → parameter.replayWindow ≤ feasible)) ∧\n    parameter.confidentialityOffset = 0 ∧ parameter.mustSecure = true) ∧\n  model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ payload iface layers trafficClass,\n    .transmit payload iface layers trafficClass ∈ events → ¬ model.GenuineControl payload →\n    ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.id = iface →\n    ∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → device.id = interface.device → device.kind = .macsec →\n    device.layer = some .inner ∧ interface.zone = .gray ∨\n      device.layer = some .outer ∧ interface.zone = .black →\n    ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.mechanism = .macsec ∧ tunnel.sender = device.id ∧ tunnel.id ∈ layers)" .
tdn:RG-028 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-028 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every MACsec device has parameters with data-delay protection, a 6000 ms lifetime, a 2000 ms normal hello interval, and a positive active hello interval no greater than 2000 ms. The replay window is 2 or the smallest feasible value; confidentiality offset is 0 and must-secure is enabled. Every relevant non-control transmission carries that device's MACsec tunnel layer." .
tdn:RG-029 rdfs:label "Inner encryption and decryption cannot be bypassed" .
tdn:RG-029 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:53\ndef msc_inner_tunnel_no_bypass {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (components : List EncryptionComponentConfiguration)\n    (outboundMACObjective inboundMACObjective : Bool) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_inner_tunnel_no_bypass { d with focus := none } model components\n    outboundMACObjective inboundMACObjective" .
tdn:RG-029 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:659\ndef TraceNoBypass (d : Deployment) (genuineControl : PayloadId → Prop)\n    (layer : Layer) (events : List NetworkEvent) : Prop :=\n  (∀ earlier middle later payload ingress receivedLayers receiveClass egress sentLayers sendClass,\n    events = earlier ++ [.receive payload ingress receivedLayers receiveClass] ++ middle ++\n      [.transmit payload egress sentLayers sendClass] ++ later →\n    ¬ genuineControl payload →\n    ∀ input ∈ d.interfaces, ∀ output ∈ d.interfaces,\n      input.id = ingress → output.id = egress → input.device = output.device →\n      d.IsLayer input.device layer →\n      (input.zone = InternalZone layer → output.zone ≠ InternalZone layer →\n        ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = layer ∧ tunnel.sender = input.device ∧\n          tunnel.id ∈ sentLayers ∧ .encrypt payload tunnel.id ∈ middle) ∧\n      (input.zone = ExternalZone layer → output.zone = InternalZone layer →\n        ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = layer ∧ tunnel.receiver = input.device ∧\n          tunnel.id ∈ receivedLayers ∧ .decrypt payload tunnel.id ∈ middle)) ∧\n  ∀ earlier later payload iface layers trafficClass,\n    events = earlier ++ [.transmit payload iface layers trafficClass] ++ later →\n    ¬ genuineControl payload →\n    ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.id = iface →\n      d.IsLayer interface.device layer → interface.zone = ExternalZone layer →\n      ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = layer ∧ tunnel.sender = interface.device ∧\n        tunnel.id ∈ layers ∧ .encrypt payload tunnel.id ∈ earlier" .
tdn:RG-029 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:693\ndef Primitive_msc_inner_tunnel_no_bypass {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (components : List EncryptionComponentConfiguration)\n    (outboundMACObjective inboundMACObjective : Bool) : Prop :=\n  ComponentConfigurationCoverage d .inner components ∧ LayerNoBypass d model .inner ∧\n  ∀ component ∈ components, d.Relevant component.id →\n    (component.mechanism = .ipsec → component.espTunnelMode = true ∧ component.associatedIPTunnel = true) ∧\n    (outboundMACObjective = true → component.outboundMACPolicy = true) ∧\n    (inboundMACObjective = true → component.inboundMACPolicy = true)" .
tdn:RG-029 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-029 tdn:requirementTranslation "The records cover every Inner encryptor and match its mechanism. For every modeled non-control packet crossing from the internal side, Inner encryption occurs before transmission and the transmitted packet carries the Inner layer. Incoming protected traffic is decrypted before passage to the internal side. IPsec uses ESP tunnel mode and an associated IP tunnel. Selected mandatory-access-control objectives must be enabled." .
tdn:RG-030 rdfs:label "Outer encryption and decryption cannot be bypassed" .
tdn:RG-030 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:59\ndef msc_outer_tunnel_no_bypass {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (components : List EncryptionComponentConfiguration)\n    (outboundMACObjective inboundMACObjective : Bool) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_outer_tunnel_no_bypass { d with focus := none } model components\n    outboundMACObjective inboundMACObjective" .
tdn:RG-030 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:659\ndef TraceNoBypass (d : Deployment) (genuineControl : PayloadId → Prop)\n    (layer : Layer) (events : List NetworkEvent) : Prop :=\n  (∀ earlier middle later payload ingress receivedLayers receiveClass egress sentLayers sendClass,\n    events = earlier ++ [.receive payload ingress receivedLayers receiveClass] ++ middle ++\n      [.transmit payload egress sentLayers sendClass] ++ later →\n    ¬ genuineControl payload →\n    ∀ input ∈ d.interfaces, ∀ output ∈ d.interfaces,\n      input.id = ingress → output.id = egress → input.device = output.device →\n      d.IsLayer input.device layer →\n      (input.zone = InternalZone layer → output.zone ≠ InternalZone layer →\n        ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = layer ∧ tunnel.sender = input.device ∧\n          tunnel.id ∈ sentLayers ∧ .encrypt payload tunnel.id ∈ middle) ∧\n      (input.zone = ExternalZone layer → output.zone = InternalZone layer →\n        ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = layer ∧ tunnel.receiver = input.device ∧\n          tunnel.id ∈ receivedLayers ∧ .decrypt payload tunnel.id ∈ middle)) ∧\n  ∀ earlier later payload iface layers trafficClass,\n    events = earlier ++ [.transmit payload iface layers trafficClass] ++ later →\n    ¬ genuineControl payload →\n    ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.id = iface →\n      d.IsLayer interface.device layer → interface.zone = ExternalZone layer →\n      ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = layer ∧ tunnel.sender = interface.device ∧\n        tunnel.id ∈ layers ∧ .encrypt payload tunnel.id ∈ earlier" .
tdn:RG-030 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:702\ndef Primitive_msc_outer_tunnel_no_bypass {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (components : List EncryptionComponentConfiguration)\n    (outboundMACObjective inboundMACObjective : Bool) : Prop :=\n  ComponentConfigurationCoverage d .outer components ∧ LayerNoBypass d model .outer ∧\n  (∀ component ∈ components, d.Relevant component.id →\n    (component.mechanism = .ipsec → component.espTunnelMode = true) ∧\n    (outboundMACObjective = true → component.outboundMACPolicy = true) ∧\n    (inboundMACObjective = true → component.inboundMACPolicy = true)) ∧\n  model.AllTraces (fun events => ∀ payload ingress layers trafficClass,\n    .receive payload ingress layers trafficClass ∈ events → ¬ model.GenuineControl payload →\n    ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.id = ingress → interface.zone = .gray →\n      d.IsLayer interface.device .outer →\n      ∃ tunnel ∈ d.tunnels, tunnel.layer = .inner ∧ layers = [tunnel.id])" .
tdn:RG-030 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-030 tdn:requirementTranslation "The records cover every Outer encryptor and match its mechanism. Every modeled non-control outward transmission carries the Outer layer after Outer encryption, and an inward crossing requires Outer decryption. IPsec uses ESP tunnel mode, and selected mandatory-access-control objectives are enabled. Non-control traffic arriving at an Outer Gray interface already carries exactly one Inner tunnel layer." .
tdn:RG-031 rdfs:label "Routing and switching limits on Encryption Components" .
tdn:RG-031 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:268\n| 31 => ∀ use ∈ records.routing, subject.Contains use.component →\n      (d.IsLayer use.component .outer → use.dynamicProtocol = false) ∧\n      (d.IsLayer use.component .inner → use.ownTunnelLookup = true ∨\n        (use.sourceComponent = use.component ∧ use.destinationComponent = use.component))" .
tdn:RG-031 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-031 tdn:requirementTranslation "Outer encryptors must not use a dynamic routing protocol. An Inner routing use must serve its own tunnel lookup or have that same component as both source and destination." .
tdn:RG-032 rdfs:label "TRANSEC under the stated deployment conditions" .
tdn:RG-032 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:65\ndef msc_transec_conditions := Primitive_msc_transec_conditions" .
tdn:RG-032 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:716\ndef Primitive_msc_transec_conditions (installations : List CoverInstallation) : Prop :=\n  TDN.Targets.msc_transec_conditions (installations.map CoverInstallation.use) ∧\n  (∀ installation ∈ installations, installation.use.enabled = installation.active) ∧\n  ∀ installation ∈ installations,\n    installation.use.publicInternet = true ∨\n      (installation.use.objectiveSelected = true ∧ installation.use.externalMACsec = true ∧\n        installation.use.outerFirewallAttached = true) →\n    installation.active = true ∧ ScheduledCoverGuarantee installation.sender" .
tdn:RG-032 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-032 tdn:requirementTranslation "The TRANSEC records must satisfy the selected conditions and agree with actual modeled activation. Public-Internet use, or the selected external-MACsec objective with an Outer Firewall, requires an active installation and its ScheduledCoverGuarantee." .
tdn:RG-033 rdfs:label "Packet sizing to control fragmentation" .
tdn:RG-033 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:67\ndef msc_packet_size_configuration {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (sizes : WireSizeModel S) (sizing : List PacketSizing) (profiles : List FragmentationProfile) : Prop :=\n  model.CoversDeployment { d with focus := none } ∧ sizes.Correspondence model sizing ∧ sizes.NoFurtherFragmentation model sizing ∧\n  PacketSizingInventory { d with focus := none } model sizing ∧\n  Primitive_msc_packet_size_configuration sizing profiles" .
tdn:RG-033 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:765\ndef Primitive_msc_packet_size_configuration (interfaces : List PacketSizing)\n    (profiles : List FragmentationProfile) : Prop :=\n  ∀ sizing ∈ interfaces,\n    (sizing.role ≠ .other →\n      0 < sizing.externalMtu ∧ 0 < sizing.payloadLimit ∧\n      (sizing.family = .ipv6 → sizing.ipv6PmtuConfigured = true) ∧\n      ∀ bytes, bytes ≤ sizing.payloadLimit → sizing.encodedSize bytes ≤ sizing.externalMtu) ∧\n    (sizing.role = .innerExternal → sizing.innerObjectiveSelected = true →\n      0 < sizing.externalMtu ∧\n      (sizing.family = .ipv6 → sizing.ipv6PmtuConfigured = true) ∧\n      ∃ profile ∈ profiles, profile.interface = sizing.interface ∧\n        profile.afterMtu = sizing.externalMtu ∧\n        (∀ bytes, 0 < bytes → bytes ≤ sizing.payloadLimit →\n          bytes ∈ profile.supportedPayloadSizes ∧\n          sizing.encodedSize bytes = bytes + profile.afterOverhead) ∧\n        profile.Reduces)" .
tdn:RG-033 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-033 tdn:requirementTranslation "The model must cover the deployment and its packet-sizing inventory. The byte-size model must agree with packet processing and show that the selected sizing avoids further fragmentation. The recorded before-and-after fragmentation profiles must also satisfy the sizing conditions." .
tdn:RG-034 rdfs:label "Outer Firewall placement for untrusted Black transport" .
tdn:RG-034 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:73\ndef msc_outer_firewall_placement := @Primitive_msc_outer_firewall_placement" .
tdn:RG-034 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:878\ndef Primitive_msc_outer_firewall_placement {Node : Type}\n    (untrustedBlack publicInternet grayFirewallRequired : Bool)\n    (edge grayConnection : Node → Node → Prop)\n    (outer firewall black grayFirewall inner : Node → Prop)\n    (insideAttachment outsideAttachment externalBlackConnection : Node → Node → Prop) : Prop :=\n  TDN.Targets.msc_outer_firewall_placement untrustedBlack publicInternet grayFirewallRequired\n    edge grayConnection outer firewall black grayFirewall inner\n    insideAttachment outsideAttachment externalBlackConnection" .
tdn:RG-034 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/Topology.lean:5\ndef msc_outer_firewall_placement {Node : Type}\n    (untrustedBlack publicInternet grayFirewallRequired : Bool)\n    (edge grayConnection : Node → Node → Prop)\n    (outer firewall black grayFirewall inner : Node → Prop)\n    (insideAttachment outsideAttachment externalBlackConnection : Node → Node → Prop) : Prop :=\n  (publicInternet = true → untrustedBlack = true) ∧\n  (∀ a b, insideAttachment a b ∨ outsideAttachment a b ∨ externalBlackConnection a b →\n    Relation.ReflTransGen edge a b) ∧\n  (if publicInternet then\n    ∀ o, outer o → ∃ f b, firewall f ∧ black b ∧\n      insideAttachment o f ∧ outsideAttachment f b\n   else ∀ o, outer o → ∃ b, black b ∧ externalBlackConnection o b) ∧\n  (untrustedBlack = true → ∀ o b, outer o → black b →\n    ¬ Relation.ReflTransGen (Waypointing.Avoiding edge firewall) o b) ∧\n  (if grayFirewallRequired then\n    ∀ o, outer o → ∃ g, grayFirewall g ∧ grayConnection o g\n   else ∀ o, outer o → ∃ i, inner i ∧ grayConnection o i)" .
tdn:RG-034 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-034 tdn:requirementTranslation "Public Internet counts as untrusted Black transport. Declared attachments must correspond to paths. Internet-connected Outer devices attach through Outer Firewalls; other Outer devices have the specified Black connection. Every Outer-to-untrusted-Black path crosses an Outer Firewall. Each Outer also has the required internal Gray connection to a Gray Firewall or Inner component." .
tdn:RG-035 rdfs:label "Permitted protocols and peers at encryption and firewall boundaries" .
tdn:RG-035 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:75\ndef msc_boundary_interface_filtering (d : Deployment) (outerFirewallRequired : Bool)\n    (firewallInternal : String → Bool) (localOuter : String → String) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_boundary_interface_filtering { d with focus := none } outerFirewallRequired\n    firewallInternal localOuter" .
tdn:RG-035 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:898\ndef Primitive_msc_boundary_interface_filtering (d : Deployment) (outerFirewallRequired : Bool)\n    (firewallInternal : String → Bool) (localOuter : String → String) : Prop :=\n  d.AddressInventoryCoherent ∧ d.ProcessingCoherent ∧ d.UDPBindingsCoherent ∧\n  ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → ∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → interface.device = device.id →\n    ((device.layer = some .outer ∧ interface.zone = .black) ∨\n      (device.layer = some .inner ∧ interface.zone = .gray) ∨\n      (device.layer = some .inner ∧ interface.zone = .red) ∨\n      (device.kind = .outerFirewall ∧ outerFirewallRequired = true)) →\n    d.BoundaryPolicyCoverage interface ∧ ∀ direction traffic, d.BoundaryAdmission device interface direction traffic →\n      (device.layer = some .outer → interface.zone = .black →\n        ((device.kind = .vpn → d.IPsecTraffic traffic ∨\n          ApprovedControl d device.id traffic) ∧\n        (device.kind = .macsec → PacketMACsec traffic.packet ∨\n          ApprovedControl d device.id traffic) ∧\n        (direction = .outbound → d.IntendedPacketPeerAt interface.id device.id traffic))) ∧\n      (device.layer = some .inner → interface.zone = .gray →\n        d.PermittedTunnelTraffic traffic ∨ AOApprovedControl d device.id traffic) ∧\n      (device.layer = some .inner → interface.zone = .red →\n        d.redService device.id traffic.packet.source (TransportServicePort traffic.packet true) ∨\n        d.redService device.id traffic.packet.destination (TransportServicePort traffic.packet false)) ∧\n      (device.kind = .outerFirewall → outerFirewallRequired = true →\n        (d.PermittedTunnelTraffic traffic ∨ ApprovedControl d device.id traffic) ∧\n        (direction = .inbound → ¬ ApprovedControl d device.id traffic →\n          if firewallInternal interface.id then\n            LocalOuterAddress d device.id (localOuter device.id) traffic.packet.source\n          else LocalOuterAddress d device.id (localOuter device.id) traffic.packet.destination))" .
tdn:RG-035 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-035 tdn:requirementTranslation "Addresses, packet processing, UDP bindings, and interface policies must agree. Admitted traffic at the specified Inner, Outer, and Outer-Firewall boundaries must match the permitted tunnel, service, or approved-control conditions. Outbound Outer traffic must use an intended peer, and Outer-Firewall ingress must use the local Outer address on the appropriate side." .
tdn:RG-036 rdfs:label "Minimal network-interface exposure" .
tdn:RG-036 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:272\n| 36 => each (fun _ record => record.enabledInterfaces = record.minimumFeasibleExposure ∧\n      ∀ interface ∈ record.unusedInterfaces, interface ∉ record.enabledInterfaces)" .
tdn:RG-036 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-036 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each component's enabled interfaces must equal its recorded minimum feasible exposure, and every recorded unused interface must be disabled." .
tdn:RG-037 rdfs:label "Outer-component third-party contact restrictions" .
tdn:RG-037 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:80\ndef msc_outer_third_party_services (d : Deployment) (objectiveSelected : String → Bool)\n    (features : List ThirdPartyFeature) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_outer_third_party_services { d with focus := none } objectiveSelected features" .
tdn:RG-037 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:932\ndef Primitive_msc_outer_third_party_services (d : Deployment) (objectiveSelected : String → Bool)\n    (features : List ThirdPartyFeature) : Prop :=\n  ∀ feature ∈ features, d.Relevant feature.device → d.IsLayer feature.device .outer → feature.canContactThirdParty = true →\n    if objectiveSelected feature.device then feature.enabled = false else\n      ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → interface.device = feature.device →\n        ∀ traffic, feature.emittedTraffic traffic →\n          ¬ d.Accepts interface.id .outbound traffic" .
tdn:RG-037 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-037 tdn:requirementTranslation "An Outer feature that can contact third parties must be disabled when the disabling objective is selected. Otherwise, every packet that feature could emit must be rejected on every relevant outbound interface." .
tdn:RG-038 rdfs:label "IP header and multicast filtering" .
tdn:RG-038 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:84\ndef msc_ip_header_and_multicast_filtering (d : Deployment)\n    (dropIPv4OptionsObjective : String → Bool) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_ip_header_and_multicast_filtering { d with focus := none } dropIPv4OptionsObjective" .
tdn:RG-038 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:957\ndef Primitive_msc_ip_header_and_multicast_filtering (d : Deployment)\n    (dropIPv4OptionsObjective : String → Bool) : Prop :=\n  (∀ device, dropIPv4OptionsObjective device = d.dropIPv4Options device) ∧\n  d.AddressInventoryCoherent ∧ d.ProcessingCoherent ∧ d.LinkPoliciesComplete ∧\n  ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → ∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → interface.device = device.id →\n    HeaderFilterApplies device interface →\n    d.PolicyCoverage interface ∧\n    ∀ traffic, d.Accepts interface.id .inbound traffic →\n      (device.layer = some .outer → interface.zone = .black →\n        traffic.multicast = false ∨ NecessaryApprovedL2Control d interface traffic) ∧\n      (device.kind = .vpn → traffic.ipVersion = some 4 → traffic.ipProtocol ∈ [6, 17, 50, 1]) ∧\n      (device.kind = .vpn → traffic.ipVersion = some 6 →\n        traffic.packet.ipv6NextHeader ∈ [50, 6, 17, 58]) ∧\n      (device.kind = .vpn → device.layer = some .outer → traffic.ipVersion = some 4 →\n        dropIPv4OptionsObjective device.id = true → traffic.packet.ipv4HeaderWords = 5)" .
tdn:RG-038 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-038 tdn:requirementTranslation "The interface policy must cover the relevant VPN and Outer interfaces. Accepted VPN traffic uses the listed IPv4 protocols or IPv6 next headers. Outer Black multicast is rejected except for the precisely modeled necessary, approved Layer-2 control traffic. When the IPv4-options objective is selected, accepted Outer VPN IPv4 packets have the ordinary five-word header." .
tdn:RG-039 rdfs:label "Outer Gray-interface allowlist and default denial" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:88\ndef msc_outer_gray_interface_policy (d : Deployment) (cdpOnGray : Bool) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_outer_gray_interface_policy { d with focus := none } cdpOnGray" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1004\ndef Primitive_msc_outer_gray_interface_policy (d : Deployment) (cdpOnGray : Bool) : Prop :=\n  d.AddressInventoryCoherent ∧ d.ProcessingCoherent ∧ d.UDPBindingsCoherent ∧\n  ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → d.IsLayer interface.device .outer → interface.zone = .gray →\n    d.PolicyCoverage interface ∧\n    (∀ direction traffic, d.Accepts interface.id direction traffic →\n      OuterGrayRestrictions d interface direction cdpOnGray traffic ∧\n      OuterPolicyAllowance d interface.device cdpOnGray traffic) ∧\n    ∀ direction hook traffic, d.PacketEligibleAt interface direction hook traffic →\n      OuterGrayRestrictions d interface direction cdpOnGray traffic →\n      OuterPolicyAllowance d interface.device cdpOnGray traffic →\n      d.AcceptsAt interface.id direction hook traffic" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:973\ndef OuterManagementInitiation (d : Deployment) (traffic : Traffic) : Prop :=\n  traffic.trafficClass = .management ∧\n    (d.grayWorkstation traffic.originator ∨\n      (d.IsLayer traffic.originator .outer ∧ traffic.service ∈ [\"logging\", \"authentication\"]))" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:978\ndef OuterTunnelAllowance (d : Deployment) (device : String) (traffic : Traffic) : Prop :=\n  (d.TunnelTraffic traffic ∨ (∃ source destination, d.CarrierInnerPair traffic source destination)) ∧\n    ((d.SameLevelInner traffic ∧ d.AppropriateInnerTunnel traffic) ∨\n      (d.grayManagementService device traffic ∧ d.GrayManagementTunnel traffic))" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:986\ndef OuterPolicyAllowance (d : Deployment) (device : String) (cdpOnGray : Bool)\n    (traffic : Traffic) : Prop :=\n  OuterTunnelAllowance d device traffic ∨\n    (cdpOnGray = true ∧ d.IsDevice device .vpn ∧ RevocationHTTP traffic) ∨\n    ((traffic.trafficClass = .management ∨ traffic.trafficClass = .control) ∧\n      d.policyApproved device traffic)" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:993\ndef OuterGrayRestrictions (d : Deployment) (interface : Interface) (direction : Direction)\n    (cdpOnGray : Bool) (traffic : Traffic) : Prop :=\n  d.HeaderEligible interface traffic ∧\n  (traffic.trafficClass = .management → OuterManagementInitiation d traffic) ∧\n  (direction = .inbound → d.reachableSource interface.id traffic.packet.source) ∧\n  (traffic.trafficClass = .protectedData → ¬ RevocationHTTP traffic →\n    d.SameLevelInner traffic ∨\n      (d.grayManagementService interface.device traffic ∧ d.GrayManagementTunnel traffic)) ∧\n  (traffic.service = \"http\" → cdpOnGray = true → d.IsDevice interface.device .vpn →\n    traffic.innerRevocation = true)" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-039 tdn:requirementTranslation "Outer Gray policies allow the specified same-level Inner tunnels, Gray-management tunnels, approved management or control traffic, and the selected Inner-revocation HTTP exception. Accepted packets also satisfy header restrictions, reachable-source checks on ingress, and the management-initiation restrictions. Every eligible packet meeting the complete modeled allowance and restrictions is accepted at its processing hook. The address, processing, UDP, and policy records must agree." .
tdn:RG-040 rdfs:label "Gray Firewall allowlist and cross-level denial" .
tdn:RG-040 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:91\ndef msc_gray_firewall_allowlist (d : Deployment) (grayFirewallRequired : Bool) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_gray_firewall_allowlist { d with focus := none } grayFirewallRequired" .
tdn:RG-040 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1021\ndef GrayPolicyAllowance (d : Deployment) (interface : Interface) (traffic : Traffic) : Prop :=\n  ((d.TunnelTraffic traffic ∨ (∃ source destination, d.CarrierInnerPair traffic source destination)) ∧\n    d.SameLevelInner traffic ∧ d.AppropriateInnerTunnel traffic) ∨ RevocationHTTP traffic ∨\n    GrayManagementAllowance d interface traffic ∨\n    (traffic.trafficClass = .control ∧ d.policyApproved interface.device traffic)" .
tdn:RG-040 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1034\ndef GrayFirewallRestrictions (d : Deployment) (interface : Interface) (direction : Direction)\n    (traffic : Traffic) : Prop :=\n  d.HeaderEligible interface traffic ∧\n  (traffic.trafficClass = .management → GrayManagementAllowance d interface traffic) ∧\n  (traffic.trafficClass = .protectedData → ¬ RevocationHTTP traffic → d.SameLevelInner traffic) ∧\n  (direction = .inbound → d.reachableSource interface.id traffic.packet.source) ∧\n  (traffic.service = \"http\" → traffic.innerRevocation = true) ∧\n  ¬ DifferentClassificationVPNs d traffic" .
tdn:RG-040 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1043\ndef Primitive_msc_gray_firewall_allowlist (d : Deployment) (grayFirewallRequired : Bool) : Prop :=\n  d.AddressInventoryCoherent ∧\n  (grayFirewallRequired = true → d.ProcessingCoherent ∧ d.UDPBindingsCoherent ∧\n    ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device →\n      d.IsDevice interface.device .grayFirewall → d.PolicyCoverage interface ∧\n        (∀ direction traffic, d.Accepts interface.id direction traffic →\n          GrayFirewallRestrictions d interface direction traffic ∧\n          GrayPolicyAllowance d interface traffic) ∧\n        ∀ direction hook traffic, d.PacketEligibleAt interface direction hook traffic →\n          d.GrayForwardPermission interface hook traffic →\n          GrayFirewallRestrictions d interface direction traffic →\n          GrayPolicyAllowance d interface traffic →\n          d.AcceptsAt interface.id direction hook traffic) ∧\n  ∀ interface ∈ d.interfaces, d.Relevant interface.device → d.IsDevice interface.device .grayFirewall →\n    ∀ direction traffic, DifferentClassificationVPNs d traffic →\n      ¬ d.Accepts interface.id direction traffic" .
tdn:RG-040 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-040 tdn:requirementTranslation "Gray Firewall policies allow the specified same-level Inner tunnels, Inner-revocation HTTP, approved control traffic, and approved management traffic on a physical management interface. Accepted traffic satisfies header, source-reachability, and classification restrictions. Eligible packets meeting the complete conditions and forwarding permission are accepted. Traffic between Inner VPNs at different classifications is always rejected." .
tdn:RG-041 rdfs:label "Control-plane approval, defaults, and service location" .
tdn:RG-041 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:274\n| 41 => each (fun device record => ControlServiceConfiguration record device)" .
tdn:RG-041 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:505\ndef ControlServiceConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) (device : Device) : Prop :=\n  ∀ service ∈ record.services, service.enabled = true →\n    (device.layer = some .inner → service.network = .red) ∧\n    (device.layer = some .outer → service.network = .gray) ∧\n    ((service.layer = 2 ∧ service.neededForOperation = true) ∨ service.aoApproved = true)" .
tdn:RG-041 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-041 tdn:requirementTranslation "An enabled control service on an Inner encryptor is attached to Red; on an Outer encryptor it is attached to Gray. Each enabled service is either necessary Layer-2 control traffic or explicitly approved by the AO." .
tdn:RG-042 rdfs:label "Layer-specific trusted time synchronization" .
tdn:RG-042 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:275\n| 42 => each (fun device _ => TrustedTimeConfiguration records.time device d)" .
tdn:RG-042 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/TimeSynchronization.lean:209\ndef TimeServiceRecord.ValidUse (record : TimeServiceRecord)\n    (observations : TimeObservationInventory) (d : Deployment) (zone : Zone)\n    (binding : TimeClockBinding) (use : TimeClockUse) : Prop :=\n  record.binding = binding.id ∧ use.binding = binding.id ∧ binding.InScope use ∧\n  use.clock = binding.clock ∧ use.clockKind = binding.clockKind ∧ use.process = binding.process ∧\n  use.executable = binding.executable ∧\n  record.source.Bound d zone ∧ observations.runtime.sourceTrusted record.source ∧\n  ∃ configuration ∈ observations.configurations,\n    configuration.id = record.configuration ∧\n    use.configuration = configuration.id ∧ configuration.clock = binding.clock ∧\n    configuration.source = record.source ∧ configuration.adjustmentEnabled = true ∧\n    configuration.observer = binding.observer ∧ binding.operatingFrom ≤ configuration.order ∧\n    use.source = record.source ∧\n    (match configuration.maximumRemainingCorrectionNanoseconds with\n      | none => True\n      | some maximum => ∃ offset, use.remainingCorrectionNanoseconds = some offset ∧\n          offset.natAbs ≤ maximum) ∧\n    (match configuration.maximumSkewMilliPpm with\n      | none => True\n      | some maximum => ∃ skew, use.skewMilliPpm = some skew ∧ skew ≤ maximum) ∧\n    ∃ update ∈ observations.updates,\n      update.id = record.update ∧ use.update = update.id ∧\n      update.configuration = configuration.id ∧ update.clock = binding.clock ∧\n      update.source = record.source ∧ update.operation.Valid ∧\n      update.process = configuration.synchronizerProcess ∧\n      (match update.operation with\n        | .correction _ _ => True\n        | .discipline process => process = configuration.synchronizerProcess) ∧\n      update.observer = binding.observer ∧ configuration.order < update.order ∧\n      update.order < use.order ∧\n      (∀ later ∈ observations.updates, later.clock = binding.clock →\n        later.observer = binding.observer → later.order ≤ use.order →\n        later.order ≤ update.order) ∧\n      ∀ invalidation ∈ observations.invalidations, invalidation.clock = binding.clock →\n        invalidation.observer = binding.observer →\n        ¬ (update.order ≤ invalidation.order ∧ invalidation.order ≤ use.order)" .
tdn:RG-042 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/TimeSynchronization.lean:246\ndef TimeConfigurationForClient (observations : TimeObservationInventory) (d : Deployment)\n    (client : TimeClient) (zone : Zone) : Prop :=\n  (∃ binding ∈ observations.bindings, binding.client = client) ∧\n  ∀ binding ∈ observations.bindings, binding.client = client →\n    (∃ use ∈ observations.uses, binding.InScope use) ∧\n    ∀ use ∈ observations.uses, binding.InScope use →\n      ∃ record ∈ observations.services, record.ValidUse observations d zone binding use" .
tdn:RG-042 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/TimeSynchronization.lean:254\ndef TrustedTimeConfiguration (observations : TimeObservationInventory)\n    (device : Device) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  ∀ client zone, client.component = device.id → client.Required d zone →\n    TimeConfigurationForClient observations d client zone" .
tdn:RG-042 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-042 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each device that requires a trusted clock source must have a recorded clock binding and at least one in-scope clock use. Every such use must match a trusted source in the required zone, an enabled synchronization configuration, and a preceding valid clock update. Configured correction and skew limits must hold, the selected update must be the latest at that use, and no intervening clock invalidation is allowed." .
tdn:RG-043 rdfs:label "Default credentials, DNS, and remote bootstrap" .
tdn:RG-043 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:276\n| 43 => context.ConfigurationDefaults subject" .
tdn:RG-043 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:499\ndef DefaultAndDNSConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  (∀ mechanism ∈ record.defaults,\n    mechanism.removed = true ∨ mechanism.currentValue ≠ mechanism.vendorValue) ∧\n  (record.dnsEnabled = true → record.dnsServers ≠ []) ∧ record.automaticRemoteBoot = false ∧\n  (record.dnsLookupDisableSelected = true → record.dnsLookupEnabled = false)" .
tdn:RG-043 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-043 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every recorded vendor-default setting is removed or changed. Enabled DNS has a server list, automatic remote boot is disabled, and selecting the DNS-lookup-disable objective disables lookups." .
tdn:RG-044 rdfs:label "Layer-specific administration and management-plane separation" .
tdn:RG-044 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:277\n| 44 => ManagementAttachmentConfiguration records d" .
tdn:RG-044 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:522\ndef ManagementSeparation (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  (∀ iface ∈ record.managementInterfaces, iface ∉ record.dataInterfaces) ∧\n  record.managementPhysicalSeparated = true ∧ record.managementCryptographicSeparated = true ∧\n  record.managementACLSeparated = true ∧ record.directNIPRConnection = false" .
tdn:RG-044 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:527\ndef ManagementAttachmentConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  records.managementDeployed = true →\n  (∃ red ∈ d.devices, red.kind = .workstation ∧\n    ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.device = red.id ∧ interface.zone = .red ∧\n      interface.managementNetwork = true) ∧\n  (∃ gray ∈ d.devices, gray.kind = .workstation ∧\n    ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.device = gray.id ∧ interface.zone = .gray ∧\n      interface.managementNetwork = true) ∧\n  ∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id →\n    ∀ record ∈ records.components, record.component = device.id →\n      ManagementSeparation record ∧\n      (∀ iface ∈ record.managementInterfaces, ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces,\n        interface.id = iface ∧ interface.device = device.id ∧ interface.managementNetwork = true) ∧\n      record.managementConnections ≠ [] ∧\n      ∀ connection ∈ record.managementConnections,\n        connection.component = device.id ∧\n        (∃ workstation ∈ d.devices, workstation.id = connection.initiatedFromAW ∧\n          workstation.kind = .workstation ∧\n          ∃ source ∈ d.interfaces, source.device = workstation.id ∧\n            source.managementNetwork = true ∧\n            ∃ target ∈ d.interfaces, target.id = connection.interface ∧\n              target.device = device.id ∧ target.managementNetwork = true ∧\n              source.zone = target.zone ∧\n              (device.layer = some .inner ∨ device.kind = .innerFirewall →\n                target.zone = .red) ∧\n              (device.layer = some .outer ∨ device.kind = .grayFirewall →\n                target.zone = .gray))" .
tdn:RG-044 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-044 tdn:requirementTranslation "When management is deployed, the deployment has both Red and Gray management workstations. Each relevant component has separate management interfaces, physical, cryptographic, and ACL separation, and no direct NIPR connection. Recorded management connections start at a workstation in the same zone. Inner encryptors and Inner Firewalls use Red management; Outer encryptors and Gray Firewalls use Gray management." .
tdn:RG-045 rdfs:label "Dedicated, protected, hardened Administrative Workstations" .
tdn:RG-045 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:278\n| 45 => each (fun device record => device.kind = .workstation →\n      WorkstationHostConfiguration records record ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .vendorAndLocalHardening (.component device.id) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .protectedFacility (.component device.id))" .
tdn:RG-045 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:555\ndef WorkstationHostConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords)\n    (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  (record.awCurrentlyUsed = false → record.awPoweredOnWhenUnused = false) ∧\n  ∀ service ∈ records.hostServices, service.host = record.awHost →\n    service.service = \"administrative-workstation\"" .
tdn:RG-045 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-045 tdn:requirementTranslation "An unused Administrative Workstation must be powered off. Every service recorded on its host must be an administrative-workstation service. The component also needs external confirmation of vendor and local hardening and a protected facility." .
tdn:RG-046 rdfs:label "Management transport protection and local exceptions" .
tdn:RG-046 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:282\n| 46 => each (fun _ record => ManagementTransportConfiguration record)" .
tdn:RG-046 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:511\ndef ManagementTransportConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.administratorAddresses = record.minimumAdministratorAddresses ∧\n  ∀ connection ∈ record.managementConnections,\n    connection.interface ∈ record.managementInterfaces ∧\n    (connection.directPhysical = true ∨\n      connection.protocol ∈ [\"ssh\", \"ipsec\", \"macsec\"] ∨\n      (connection.protocol = \"tls\" ∧ connection.tlsMajor = 1 ∧ 2 ≤ connection.tlsMinor)) ∧\n    (connection.crossesBlack = true →\n      2 ≤ connection.approvedEncryptionLayers ∧\n      (connection.localDedicatedLAN = true → connection.sameVLAN = true))" .
tdn:RG-046 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-046 tdn:requirementTranslation "Administrator addresses are limited to the recorded minimum set. Each management connection uses a management interface and either a direct physical connection, SSH, IPsec, MACsec, or TLS 1.2 or later within major version 1. Connections crossing Black use at least two approved encryption layers. A connection marked as a local dedicated LAN must then also remain on the same VLAN." .
tdn:RG-047 rdfs:label "Administrator authentication and individual credentials" .
tdn:RG-047 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/Administration.lean:59\ndef msc_administrator_authentication (certificateObjective nistObjective : Bool)\n    (events : List AdminEvent) (accounts : List AdministrativeAccount)\n    (sessions : List AdministrativeSession) (awAdministrators : List Nat) : Prop :=\n  (∀ event ∈ events, event.kind = .operation →\n    ∃ authentication ∈ events,\n      MatchingAdministratorAuthentication certificateObjective nistObjective events accounts sessions\n        authentication event) ∧\n  (∀ account ∈ accounts, account.credential ≠ \"\" ∧\n    (account.workstationAccount = true → account.groupAccount = false)) ∧\n  (∀ person ∈ awAdministrators, ∃ account ∈ accounts,\n    account.person = person ∧ account.workstationAccount = true) ∧\n  ∀ a ∈ accounts, a.workstationAccount = true →\n    ∀ b ∈ accounts, b.workstationAccount = true →\n      a.person ≠ b.person → a.credential ≠ b.credential" .
tdn:RG-047 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:94\ndef msc_administrator_authentication (d : Deployment)\n    (certificateObjective nistObjective : Bool) (events : List AdminEvent)\n    (accounts : List AdministrativeAccount) (sessions : List AdministrativeSession)\n    (awAdministrators : List Nat) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_administrator_authentication { d with focus := none } certificateObjective\n    nistObjective events accounts sessions awAdministrators" .
tdn:RG-047 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1060\ndef Primitive_msc_administrator_authentication (d : Deployment)\n    (certificateObjective nistObjective : Bool) (events : List AdminEvent)\n    (accounts : List AdministrativeAccount) (sessions : List AdministrativeSession)\n    (awAdministrators : List Nat) : Prop :=\n  TDN.Targets.msc_administrator_authentication certificateObjective nistObjective\n    events accounts sessions awAdministrators ∧\n  ∀ event ∈ events, event.kind = .authentication →\n    (certificateObjective = true → d.authority.certificateCNSACompliant event.credential) ∧\n    (nistObjective = true → d.authority.authenticationConformsToNIST80063 event.credential)" .
tdn:RG-047 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete model proof reviewed" .
tdn:RG-047 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every administrative operation has a matching authentication event satisfying the session, account, and ordering conditions. Account credentials are nonempty. Workstation accounts are individual, every listed workstation administrator has one, and different people use different credentials. Selected certificate and NIST objectives add the corresponding credential-approval conditions." .
tdn:RG-048 rdfs:label "Authorized provisioning and initial certificate requests" .
tdn:RG-048 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:283\n| 48 => each (fun device _ => ProvisioningConfiguration records d device.id)" .
tdn:RG-048 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:562\ndef ProvisioningConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment)\n    (component : String) : Prop :=\n  (∀ certificate ∈ records.certificates, certificate.subject = component →\n    certificate.vendorDefault = false → certificate.selfSigned = false →\n    certificate.proprietary = false →\n    ∃ provision ∈ records.provisioning, provision.component = component ∧\n      provision.certificate = certificate.id) ∧\n  ∀ provision ∈ records.provisioning, provision.component = component →\n    d.authority.securityAdministrator provision.administrator ∧\n    provision.keyGeneratedOnComponent = true ∧ provision.csr ≠ \"\" ∧\n    provision.securePhysicalArea = true ∧ provision.outOfBand = true ∧\n    provision.provisionedAt < provision.firstUsedAt ∧\n    (∀ authentication ∈ records.authentications,\n      authentication.input.credential = provision.certificate →\n      provision.provisionedAt < authentication.input.time) ∧\n    (∃ certificate ∈ records.certificates, certificate.id = provision.certificate ∧\n      certificate.subject = component ∧ certificate.issuer = provision.ca) ∧\n    (∃ authority ∈ d.devices, authority.id = provision.ca ∧\n      authority.kind = .certificationAuthority ∧ d.keyManagementCA component authority.id)" .
tdn:RG-048 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-048 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every eligible non-default certificate has a provisioning record. Each provisioning record names an authorized administrator, a key generated on the component, a nonempty certificate request, and a secure out-of-band physical setup. Provisioning precedes first use and recorded authentications with the certificate. The certificate and its assigned CA must match the component and deployment records." .
tdn:RG-049 rdfs:label "Personnel clearance and Outer administration" .
tdn:RG-049 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:284\n| 49 => external [.authorizedAdministratorClearance, .outerAdministratorClearance]" .
tdn:RG-049 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-049 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations of the required administrator clearances, including Outer administration." .
tdn:RG-050 rdfs:label "SIEM placement, collection, alerting, and log transport" .
tdn:RG-050 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:285\n| 50 => SIEMConfiguration records d" .
tdn:RG-050 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:588\ndef SIEMConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (d : Deployment) : Prop :=\n  ∀ device ∈ d.devices, d.Relevant device.id → ∀ zone,\n    ComponentMonitoringZone d device zone →\n    (∃ siem ∈ d.devices, siem.kind = .siem ∧\n      ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.device = siem.id ∧\n        (interface.zone = zone ∨ (zone = .gray ∧ interface.zone = .red))) →\n    ∀ source ∈ records.components, source.component = device.id →\n    ∃ receiver ∈ d.devices, receiver.kind = .siem ∧ source.siem = some receiver.id ∧\n      ∃ interface ∈ d.interfaces, interface.device = receiver.id ∧\n        source.siemZone = some interface.zone ∧\n        (interface.zone = zone ∨\n          (zone = .gray ∧ interface.zone = .red ∧ source.approvedCrossDomainPath = true)) ∧\n        source.loggingEnabled = true ∧\n        ∃ target ∈ records.components, target.component = receiver.id ∧\n          device.id ∈ target.collectedLogSources ∧ device.id ∈ target.analyzedLogSources ∧\n          target.alerts ≠ [] ∧\n          (zone = .red → source.flowLoggingEnabled = true ∧\n            device.id ∈ target.collectedFlowSources ∧ device.id ∈ target.analyzedFlowSources) ∧\n          (device.layer = some .outer ∨ device.kind = .grayFirewall →\n            \"unexpected-boundary-traffic-drop\" ∈ target.alerts)" .
tdn:RG-050 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-050 tdn:requirementTranslation "When a SIEM is available for the required monitoring zone, the component must log to a recorded SIEM that collects and analyzes its logs and has alerts. Red monitoring also collects and analyzes flows. Moving Gray logs to a Red SIEM needs an approved cross-domain path. Outer components and Gray Firewalls need an unexpected-boundary-traffic-drop alert." .
tdn:RG-051 rdfs:label "Cross Domain Solution approval conditions" .
tdn:RG-051 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:286\n| 51 => ∀ solution ∈ records.crossDomainSolutions,\n      records.external.Confirms .crossDomainDoDI (.component solution) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .crossDomainConnectionGuide (.component solution) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .crossDomainOfficialBaseline (.component solution)" .
tdn:RG-051 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-051 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every listed Cross Domain Solution needs external confirmations of the specified DoDI, connection-guide, and official-baseline requirements." .
tdn:RG-052 rdfs:label "Physical protection, authorized access, and disposal" .
tdn:RG-052 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:290\n| 52 => each (fun device _ =>\n      (device.kind ≠ .outerFirewall →\n        records.external.Confirms .grayPhysicalProtection (.component device.id)) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .authorizedPhysicalAccess (.component device.id) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .classifiedDisposalOrAODeclassification (.component device.id) ∧\n      (device.kind = .macsec →\n        records.external.Confirms .macsecConfigurationProtection (.component device.id)))" .
tdn:RG-052 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-052 tdn:requirementTranslation "Components need external confirmations for authorized physical access and classified disposal or approved declassification. Every component except an Outer Firewall also needs Gray physical-protection confirmation; MACsec components need configuration-protection confirmation." .
tdn:RG-053 rdfs:label "Parallel Inner components and distinct Outer internal interfaces" .
tdn:RG-053 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:297\n| 53 => (∀ first ∈ records.attachments, ∀ second ∈ records.attachments,\n      first.outer = second.outer → first.inner ≠ second.inner →\n      first.serialPredecessor = none ∧ second.serialPredecessor = none ∧\n      first.vlanTrunk = false ∧ second.vlanTrunk = false ∧\n      (first.redNetwork ≠ second.redNetwork →\n        first.outerPhysicalInterface ≠ second.outerPhysicalInterface))" .
tdn:RG-053 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-053 tdn:requirementTranslation "Inner components sharing an Outer must be parallel: no serial predecessor and no VLAN trunk in the recorded attachments. Distinct Red networks must use distinct Outer physical interfaces." .
tdn:RG-054 rdfs:label "Interoperable components across communicating sites" .
tdn:RG-054 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:101\ndef msc_site_interoperability {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (requiredSitePairs : List (String × String)) (selected : List Interoperation)\n    (domain : PayloadDomain) : Prop :=\n  Primitive_msc_site_interoperability { d with focus := none } model requiredSitePairs selected domain" .
tdn:RG-054 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1162\ndef Primitive_msc_site_interoperability {S A : Type} (d : Deployment) (model : ExecutionModel S A)\n    (requiredSitePairs : List (String × String)) (selected : List Interoperation)\n    (domain : PayloadDomain) : Prop :=\n  model.CoversDeployment d ∧ RequiredSitePairsBound d requiredSitePairs ∧\n  SiteLayerInteroperationCoverage requiredSitePairs selected ∧\n  InteroperationInventory d selected ∧ InteroperationTransfers d model selected domain" .
tdn:RG-054 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-054 tdn:requirementTranslation "Required site pairs must be bound to the deployment and have an interoperation choice for each layer. Choices cover intended peers and recorded tunnels. For each relevant choice, matching forward and reverse tunnels must support the modeled payload domain in both directions." .
tdn:RG-055 rdfs:label "Firewall requirements when combining capability packages" .
tdn:RG-055 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:303\n| 55 => (records.combinedSolutionRequiresGrayFirewall = true →\n      ∃ firewall ∈ d.devices, firewall.kind = .grayFirewall) ∧\n      (records.combinedEndUserSolution = true ↔ context.companionFirewalls ≠ []) ∧\n      ∀ companion ∈ context.companionFirewalls, companion.Requirements d records" .
tdn:RG-055 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-055 tdn:requirementTranslation "Combined solutions must include a Gray Firewall when required. A combined end-user solution must have companion-firewall records, and every such record must satisfy its associated requirements." .
tdn:RG-056 rdfs:label "Approved physical paths out of Red Networks" .
tdn:RG-056 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:106\ndef msc_approved_red_egress_paths {S A : Type} (d : Deployment)\n    (red outside : String → Prop) (conformingMSC aoApprovedProtection : String → Prop)\n    (solutions : List (CPContext S A)) : Prop :=\n  MSCReferencesClosed solutions ∧\n  (∀ solution, conformingMSC solution → ∃ context ∈ solutions,\n    context.solution = solution ∧ context.AllApplicableDuties (.solution solution)) ∧\n  RedEgressCore { d with focus := none } red outside conformingMSC aoApprovedProtection" .
tdn:RG-056 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/DirectSpecifications.lean:1169\ndef RedEgressCore (d : Deployment)\n    (red outside : String → Prop) (conformingMSC aoApprovedProtection : String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  (∀ solution, aoApprovedProtection solution → d.authority.aoApprovedTransitSolution solution) ∧\n  ∀ source destination, red source → outside destination →\n    ¬ Relation.ReflTransGen (Waypointing.Avoiding d.DeviceAdjacent\n      (fun node => conformingMSC node ∨ aoApprovedProtection node)) source destination" .
tdn:RG-056 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-056 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every modeled Red-to-outside path must pass through a conforming MSC solution or approved alternative protection. Approval must be backed by the authority record. Referenced MSC solutions must have supplied contexts satisfying all applicable duties, and their further MSC references must be accounted for." .
tdn:RG-057 rdfs:label "Operational security updates and TEMPEST policy" .
tdn:RG-057 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:307\n| 57 => each (fun device _ =>\n      ∀ duty ∈ [.aoVirusUpdatePolicy, .criticalPatchTesting, .localPatchingPolicy, .tempest],\n        records.external.Confirms duty (.component device.id))" .
tdn:RG-057 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-057 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each component needs external confirmations of the required antivirus-update policy, critical-patch testing, local patching policy, and TEMPEST duties." .
tdn:RG-058 rdfs:label "Hardware inventory and available baseline configuration" .
tdn:RG-058 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:310\n| 58 => each (fun device _ =>\n      records.external.Confirms .authorizedHardwareInventory (.component device.id) ∧\n      records.external.Confirms .baselineAvailableToAuditor (.component device.id))" .
tdn:RG-058 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-058 tdn:requirementTranslation "Each component needs external confirmations that its hardware inventory is authorized and its baseline configuration is available to the auditor." .
tdn:RG-059 rdfs:label "Procurement documentation excludes classified-protection purpose" .
tdn:RG-059 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:313\n| 59 => external [.procurementPurposeExclusion]" .
tdn:RG-059 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-059 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmation that procurement documentation follows the restriction on mentioning the classified-protection purpose." .
tdn:RG-060 rdfs:label "Annual and NSA-authorized compliance audits" .
tdn:RG-060 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:314\n| 60 => external [.nsaAuditPermission, .nsaAuditCooperation, .annualAOAudit, .annualAuditResultsReview]" .
tdn:RG-060 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-060 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations for NSA audit permission and cooperation, the annual AO audit, and review of its results." .
tdn:RG-061 rdfs:label "Registration, approval, annual renewal, and version updates" .
tdn:RG-061 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:315\n| 61 => external [.nsaRegistrationApproval, .aoRegistrationPackage, .annualRenewal,\n      .registrationChanges, .versionMigrationDeadline]" .
tdn:RG-061 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-061 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations for registration approval, the AO package, annual renewal, reported changes, and the version-migration deadline." .
tdn:RG-062 rdfs:label "Audit retention, storage monitoring, backup, and continuity" .
tdn:RG-062 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:317\n| 62 => each (fun device _ => AuditRetentionConfiguration records device.id) ∧\n      external [.incidentResponseGuidance, .auditLowSpacePlan, .auditOffloadPlan,\n        .auditOverflowPlan, .auditPowerPlan]" .
tdn:RG-062 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:628\ndef AuditRetentionConfiguration (records : TechnicalDutyRecords) (component : String) : Prop :=\n  (∀ event ∈ records.audits, event.component = component →\n    event.time + 365 * 86400 ≤ event.retainedUntil ∧\n    ∃ backup ∈ event.backedUpAt, event.time ≤ backup) ∧\n  (∃ storage ∈ records.storage, storage.component = component ∧\n    (∀ year quarter,\n      CalendarQuarterStart year quarter < storage.operatingUntil →\n      storage.operatingFrom < CalendarQuarterEnd year quarter →\n      ∃ checked ∈ storage.capacityCheckedAt,\n        CalendarQuarterStart year quarter ≤ checked ∧\n        checked < CalendarQuarterEnd year quarter ∧\n        storage.operatingFrom ≤ checked ∧ checked ≤ storage.operatingUntil) ∧\n    storage.warningOnLowSpace = true ∧ storage.offloadEnabled = true ∧\n    storage.overflowHandling ≠ \"\" ∧ storage.powerLossHandling ≠ \"\") ∧\n  records.external.Confirms .frequentAuditOffload (.component component)" .
tdn:RG-062 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-062 tdn:requirementTranslation "Recorded audit events are retained for at least 365 days and have a backup at or after the event. Storage capacity is checked during every calendar quarter overlapping operation. Low-space warning and offload are enabled, and overflow and power-loss handling are recorded. Frequent offload and the required incident-response and storage plans also need external confirmation." .
tdn:RG-063 rdfs:label "Infrastructure authentication alternatives" .
tdn:RG-063 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:320\n| 63 => each (fun _ record => if record.passwordAlternativeSelected then\n      record.domainAuthenticationService.isSome = true else 112 ≤ record.infrastructureSecretEntropyBits)" .
tdn:RG-063 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-063 tdn:requirementTranslation "If the password alternative is selected, a domain authentication service must be recorded. Otherwise, the recorded infrastructure secret must have at least 112 bits of entropy." .
tdn:RG-064 rdfs:label "Incident triggers, required report fields, and reporting deadline" .
tdn:RG-064 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:322\n| 64 => external [.incidentDeadlineAndChannel, .incidentRequiredFields,\n      .reportSecurityFailure, .reportClassifiedCompromise, .reportMaliciousGrayTraffic,\n      .reportUnauthorizedClassifiedAccess, .reportUnauthorizedDestination,\n      .reportMaliciousConfigurationChange, .reportUnauthorizedPrivilegeEscalation,\n      .reportConcurrentCertificateReuse, .reportMaliciousPhysicalTampering,\n      .reportProtectionLayerFailure, .reportSignificantServiceDegradation,\n      .reportOuterConnectionDiscrepancy, .reportInnerConnectionDiscrepancy]" .
tdn:RG-064 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-064 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations for the reporting deadline and channel, required report fields, and each listed kind of security or service incident." .
tdn:RG-065 rdfs:label "Separation of administrative and auditing personnel" .
tdn:RG-065 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:329\n| 65 => external [.differentAdministratorAndAuditor, .differentRedAndGrayAdministrators] ∧\n      (records.optionalRoleMACSelected = true → external [.optionalRoleMAC])" .
tdn:RG-065 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-065 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations that administrator and auditor duties are separated and that Red and Gray administrators are different. Selecting optional role-based mandatory access control adds its confirmation requirement." .
tdn:RG-066 rdfs:label "Personnel training and physical tamper inspections" .
tdn:RG-066 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:331\n| 66 => external [.securityTraining, .tamperInspection]" .
tdn:RG-066 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-066 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations of security training and physical tamper inspection." .
tdn:RG-067 rdfs:label "Revocation or CAK destruction before disposal" .
tdn:RG-067 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:332\n| 67 => each (fun device record => RevocationBeforeDisposal record\n      (records.certificates.any (fun certificate => certificate.subject == device.id))\n      (d.preSharedCAKAuthenticated device.id))" .
tdn:RG-067 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:644\ndef RevocationBeforeDisposal (record : ComponentDutyRecord)\n    (usesCertificate usesCAK : Bool) : Prop :=\n  ∀ disposed, record.disposedAt = some disposed →\n    (usesCertificate = true →\n      ∃ initiated, record.credentialRevocationInitiatedAt = some initiated ∧ initiated < disposed) ∧\n    (usesCAK = true →\n      ∃ initiated, record.cakDestructionInitiatedAt = some initiated ∧ initiated < disposed)" .
tdn:RG-067 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-067 tdn:requirementTranslation "For a recorded disposal, certificate-revocation initiation must precede disposal when certificates are used. CAK-destruction initiation must precede disposal when a pre-shared CAK is used." .
tdn:RG-068 rdfs:label "Security Administrator operational duties" .
tdn:RG-068 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:335\n| 68 => external [.administratorMaintainsMonitorsControls, .administratorLatestCriticalUpdates,\n      .administratorIncidentDocumentationReporting, .administratorLogisticSupport,\n      .administratorAuxiliaryDeviceDefenses, .administratorVersionCompliance]" .
tdn:RG-068 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-068 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations of the Security Administrator's maintenance, updates, incident reporting, logistical support, auxiliary-device defenses, and version-compliance duties." .
tdn:RG-069 rdfs:label "Auditor review duties and access boundary" .
tdn:RG-069 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:338\n| 69 => external [.auditorReviewsActionsAndEvents, .auditorOnlyAdministrationAccess,\n      .auditorManagesLogs, .auditorIncidentDocumentationReporting, .auditorCapabilitySurvey]" .
tdn:RG-069 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-069 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations of the Auditor's review, restricted administration access, log management, incident reporting, and capability-survey duties." .
tdn:RG-070 rdfs:label "Optional Integrator involvement and duty scope" .
tdn:RG-070 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:340\n| 70 => True" .
tdn:RG-070 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-070 tdn:requirementTranslation "The current shared Lean branch is True, so it adds no condition for optional Integrator duties. There is no substantive proof obligation in that branch." .
tdn:RG-071 rdfs:label "AO authorization evidence and lifecycle control" .
tdn:RG-071 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:341\n| 71 => external [.assessmentAuthorization, .assessmentResultsToAO, .aoImplementationVerification,\n      .lifecycleAOConfigurationControl, .lifecycleAORequiredUpdates,\n      .externalEngagementVariants, .compromiseRevocation, .nsaRiskAssessmentToAO]" .
tdn:RG-071 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-071 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations for assessment and authorization, AO review and implementation verification, lifecycle configuration and update control, external engagements, compromise revocation, and risk assessment." .
tdn:RG-072 rdfs:label "Whole-solution testing and preserved results" .
tdn:RG-072 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:344\n| 72 => external [.testingAnnex, .capabilityTestCoverage, .blackGrayBoxTests,\n      .testDiscrepancyDocumentation, .testBaselineDocumentation,\n      .testPlanAOAdditionalRequirements, .testArtifactsAndAOReport]" .
tdn:RG-072 tdn:requirementStatus "Assigned to direct checks" .
tdn:RG-072 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmations that the required tests, coverage, discrepancy records, baseline, test plan, and preserved results and AO report exist." .
tdn:RG-073 rdfs:label "Objective software and firmware signing algorithms" .
tdn:RG-073 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:347\n| 73 => each (fun _ record => SigningConfiguration record)" .
tdn:RG-073 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDutyRecords.lean:652\ndef SigningConfiguration (record : ComponentDutyRecord) : Prop :=\n  record.signatureObjectiveSelected = true →\n    record.softwareSigningAlgorithms ≠ [] ∧\n    ∀ algorithm ∈ record.softwareSigningAlgorithms, algorithm.Approved" .
tdn:RG-073 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-073 tdn:requirementTranslation "When the signing objective is selected, the record contains at least one software-signing algorithm and every listed algorithm satisfies the modeled Approved condition." .
tdn:RG-074 rdfs:label "Redundant component and load-balancing permission" .
tdn:RG-074 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CompleteSpecifications.lean:114\ndef msc_redundant_component_permission {S A : Type} (context : CPContext S A)\n    (redundant : String → Prop) : Prop :=\n  ∀ device ∈ context.deployment.devices, redundant device.id →\n    (¬ context.deployment.OrdinaryGray device.id ∨\n      context.deployment.standaloneEncapsulator device.id) →\n    context.AllApplicableDuties (.component device.id)" .
tdn:RG-074 tdn:requirementStatus "Complete proof unfinished" .
tdn:RG-074 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every selected redundant component must satisfy all applicable component duties whenever it is outside ordinary Gray scope or is a standalone encapsulator. The condition applies separately to each selected redundant device." .
tdn:RG-075 rdfs:label "Optional additional controls and screening-router scope" .
tdn:RG-075 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:349\n| 75 => (∀ router ∈ records.selectedScreeningRouters,\n      ∃ device ∈ d.devices, device.id = router ∧ device.layer = none)" .
tdn:RG-075 tdn:requirementStatus "Permission or applicability condition" .
tdn:RG-075 tdn:requirementTranslation "Every selected screening router must exist in the device inventory and have no encryption-layer assignment." .
tdn:RG-076 rdfs:label "CP user legal undertaking and disclaimer" .
tdn:RG-076 tdn:requirementCode "TDN/Targets/CPDuties.lean:351\n| 76 => external [.legalUndertaking]" .
tdn:RG-076 tdn:requirementStatus "Requires external evidence" .
tdn:RG-076 tdn:requirementTranslation "The context needs external confirmation of the legal undertaking. The Lean branch records that confirmation as an external input." .
